1
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,781
(Leaving for Chiang Mai today)

2
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:59,518
(Their Bangkok lodging, 5:00 a.m.)

3
00:01:59,887 --> 00:02:01,420
What time did you get up?

4
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:03,723
Honestly, I barely slept.

5
00:02:03,724 --> 00:02:07,160
I couldn't stop thinking...

6
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:11,664
about the bell
and that woman's blank face.

7
00:02:12,766 --> 00:02:14,066
Same here.

8
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:15,401
I didn't sleep well at all.

9
00:02:16,671 --> 00:02:19,772
- And I kept hearing that moktak.
- I know.

10
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:20,774
Really?

11
00:02:22,276 --> 00:02:23,710
That was creepy too.

12
00:02:23,911 --> 00:02:25,145
I need to buy some salt.

13
00:02:26,347 --> 00:02:27,614
We should catch a taxi.

14
00:02:28,081 --> 00:02:30,582
Right. Let's grab one.

15
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,252
The taxi is here.

16
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:34,487
- Okay.
- Okay.

17
00:02:37,791 --> 00:02:39,625
Wait! Our suitcase.

18
00:02:40,161 --> 00:02:41,093
Our suitcase.

19
00:02:41,462 --> 00:02:43,129
My shoes are...

20
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:45,165
(Making sure not to leave the suitcase)

21
00:02:45,166 --> 00:02:46,500
They're still wet.

22
00:02:47,434 --> 00:02:49,101
Hello.

23
00:02:49,803 --> 00:02:51,237
Just one suitcase.

24
00:02:51,572 --> 00:02:52,539
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

25
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,607
I'll take the front seat.

26
00:02:55,909 --> 00:02:57,209
Okay.

27
00:03:00,147 --> 00:03:01,080
Here we go.

28
00:03:01,882 --> 00:03:04,283
- Here we go.
- Off we go.

29
00:03:04,418 --> 00:03:07,387
- We're going to the airport, right?
- Yes.

30
00:03:07,388 --> 00:03:10,289
(Off to Suvarnabhumi Airport)

31
00:03:11,758 --> 00:03:14,493
Look at all the skyscrapers.

32
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:16,328
This is downtown Bangkok.

33
00:03:16,964 --> 00:03:18,364
This is downtown Bangkok.

34
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:19,265
Yep.

35
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:21,834
(Driving on...)

36
00:03:21,835 --> 00:03:24,136
(and on)

37
00:03:24,671 --> 00:03:26,839
(The sun rises.)

38
00:03:28,442 --> 00:03:29,509
(Arriving at the airport)

39
00:03:29,510 --> 00:03:30,576
We're already here.

40
00:03:33,113 --> 00:03:34,380
We made it to the airport.

41
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:35,514
(Suvarnabhumi Airport)

42
00:03:35,515 --> 00:03:36,615
Thank you.

43
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:39,552
Chiang Mai, here we come.

44
00:03:42,356 --> 00:03:44,924
(Checking in their suitcase)

45
00:03:45,526 --> 00:03:47,393
(Struggling)

46
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,899
- Hello.
- Hello.

47
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,001
Saying goodbye to Bangkok now.

48
00:03:56,537 --> 00:03:57,722
You're way too close.

49
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:01,173
- Bangkok, check!
- Leaving Bangkok behind.

50
00:04:01,174 --> 00:04:03,041
Now we're off to Chiang Mai.

51
00:04:03,611 --> 00:04:04,644
(Off to Chiang Mai, the mountain city)

52
00:04:04,645 --> 00:04:07,046
We're going to see elephants!

53
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:08,914
Elephants!

54
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:14,061
I'm going to give the elephants
a good scrub...

55
00:04:14,086 --> 00:04:15,821
with the brush I brought.

56
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:18,124
Why would you use that on elephants?

57
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:20,592
True. You should try it out first.

58
00:04:20,727 --> 00:04:22,262
Let me test it out first.

59
00:04:22,429 --> 00:04:23,829
(Almost tested it on an elephant first)

60
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,765
You really want to scrub
an elephant with that?

61
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:26,832
I do!

62
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:30,369
I'm just so excited to see the elephants.

63
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,905
She's thrilled to meet them.

64
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:33,706
She loves connecting with nature.

65
00:04:33,707 --> 00:04:35,441
(Laughs)

66
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:37,843
The video we posted yesterday
hit over a million views!

67
00:04:37,844 --> 00:04:40,179
(No way!)

68
00:04:43,584 --> 00:04:45,718
To keep up the momentum,

69
00:04:45,719 --> 00:04:47,086
we have to make...

70
00:04:47,087 --> 00:04:48,521
at least five videos today.

71
00:04:48,522 --> 00:04:51,357
Yesterday, Harimu and I kept...

72
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:53,359
- Won Ji, you doing okay?
- I'm good!

73
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:55,895
I'm ready to roll now.

74
00:04:56,297 --> 00:04:59,465
You mentioned earlier
that you've been to Chiang Mai four times.

75
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:00,366
Right.

76
00:05:00,367 --> 00:05:01,867
- How was it?
- I went pretty recently.

77
00:05:01,868 --> 00:05:04,536
There are tons
of little weekend flea markets.

78
00:05:04,537 --> 00:05:06,538
Today is Sunday,
but we won't make it in time.

79
00:05:06,539 --> 00:05:08,108
There are so many good food spots too.

80
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:10,108
You mentioned a noodle place earlier.

81
00:05:10,109 --> 00:05:11,844
There's a noodle spot there I really love.

82
00:05:11,845 --> 00:05:14,280
We can order three bowls of noodles...

83
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:17,283
then head to an air-conditioned cafe
and grab some iced coffee.

84
00:05:17,551 --> 00:05:19,485
- That sounds like perfection.
- Perfect.

85
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:20,686
Pure paradise.

86
00:05:21,021 --> 00:05:22,289
Can we get our travel budget?

87
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:24,757
- Come to think of it...
- Here's your daily budget...

88
00:05:24,758 --> 00:05:26,192
with yesterday's bonus added.

89
00:05:27,928 --> 00:05:29,162
Treasurer!

90
00:05:29,163 --> 00:05:30,530
(Treasurer Harimu takes the budget.)

91
00:05:31,131 --> 00:05:32,532
If we open it right here...

92
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:35,768
We might get targeted.

93
00:05:35,769 --> 00:05:36,635
Let's not flash our cash.

94
00:05:36,636 --> 00:05:39,138
It's definitely not enough money
to put us in danger.

95
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,408
Let's count how much we have left...

96
00:05:42,542 --> 00:05:44,113
- once we get to our place.
- Let's see...

97
00:05:44,138 --> 00:05:45,454
- Yeah.
- how much we each have left.

98
00:05:45,479 --> 00:05:47,513
We should head in.
That's our boarding call, right?

99
00:05:47,538 --> 00:05:49,372
Let's go!

100
00:05:49,592 --> 00:05:50,692
I look so innocent today.

101
00:05:50,717 --> 00:05:52,494
My vibe today is totally fresh and pure.

102
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:53,987
I feel like I'm going on a blind date...

103
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:55,899
with elephants.

104
00:05:55,924 --> 00:05:57,489
(Off to a blind date)

105
00:05:57,758 --> 00:06:00,692
(Boarding the shuttle bus)

106
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:02,795
I love our poses.

107
00:06:02,796 --> 00:06:04,430
Could you take a photo of us?

108
00:06:04,431 --> 00:06:06,299
- Let's do this pose.
- Lean a little to the side.

109
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:10,035
(Lean a little?)

110
00:06:10,904 --> 00:06:11,871
Okay!

111
00:06:12,638 --> 00:06:15,274
Love the vibe.

112
00:06:15,442 --> 00:06:16,409
Looks great.

113
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:17,276
Wait.

114
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:19,713
What if we get scouted
for a magazine shoot?

115
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,581
(Getting ahead of herself again)

116
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:25,451
- Hello.
- Hello.

117
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:28,787
We're finally heading to Chiang Mai.

118
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:32,091
I'm so excited to meet the elephants.

119
00:06:32,793 --> 00:06:34,994
I'm going to give them nicknames.

120
00:06:35,429 --> 00:06:37,797
Chiang Mai, here we come!

121
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:41,534
(Peekaboo)

122
00:06:44,004 --> 00:06:48,107
(A 1-hour-20-minute flight
from Bangkok to Chiang Mai)

123
00:06:48,608 --> 00:06:52,244
(Heading from southern
to northern Thailand)

124
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,915
(Touching down in Chiang Mai)

125
00:06:56,950 --> 00:07:00,052
(Chiang Mai International Airport)

126
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:03,021
Let's go.

127
00:07:03,156 --> 00:07:05,891
Hello, everyone!
We've arrived in Chiang Mai!

128
00:07:06,193 --> 00:07:07,794
- Chiang Mai!
- Chiang Mai!

129
00:07:09,029 --> 00:07:11,897
(Where beautiful nature meets
traditional culture)

130
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:15,167
(A city rich in Buddhist heritage)

131
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:18,604
(A vibrant gem...)

132
00:07:18,905 --> 00:07:21,640
(in northern Thailand)

133
00:07:21,842 --> 00:07:23,810
(Chiang Mai)

134
00:07:24,044 --> 00:07:25,878
Chiang Mai, long time no see!

135
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:27,147
Chiang Mai!

136
00:07:27,148 --> 00:07:28,614
By the way,

137
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:31,951
it's way less humid here than in Bangkok.

138
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:32,985
Yes.

139
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:35,154
We're in northern Thailand now, right?

140
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:37,690
Yep, northern Thailand.

141
00:07:38,024 --> 00:07:40,425
So now...

142
00:07:40,426 --> 00:07:42,561
- Are we heading to our place?
- Sounds like a plan.

143
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:43,628
What was the address again?

144
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,130
How should we get there?

145
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:46,664
Let's just take a taxi.

146
00:07:46,665 --> 00:07:48,333
- We could do that.
- Okay.

147
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:50,068
In Chiang Mai,

148
00:07:50,069 --> 00:07:52,104
they have this local shared pickup
called a songthaew.

149
00:07:52,215 --> 00:07:53,047
Songthao?

150
00:07:53,072 --> 00:07:54,473
- Songthaew.
- Never heard of that before.

151
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,374
Songthaew?

152
00:07:55,542 --> 00:07:57,877
It's like a pickup truck
with bench seating in the back.

153
00:07:57,878 --> 00:07:59,078
Let's take that then!

154
00:07:59,212 --> 00:08:00,779
- Shall we?
- Sounds fun!

155
00:08:00,881 --> 00:08:03,181
They didn't have those in Bangkok.

156
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:05,918
I'm not sure what the going rate is,

157
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:08,011
but let's haggle once we spot one.

158
00:08:08,421 --> 00:08:10,188
(Looking around)

159
00:08:11,391 --> 00:08:12,391
Is that one?

160
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:13,625
That red truck over there.

161
00:08:13,626 --> 00:08:15,093
- That one.
- The red one!

162
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:17,396
Songthaew!

163
00:08:17,697 --> 00:08:19,097
Excuse me, sir!

164
00:08:22,769 --> 00:08:24,436
Hello!

165
00:08:24,605 --> 00:08:26,572
(Showing the address before negotiating)

166
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:29,708
- How many people?
- Four.

167
00:08:31,378 --> 00:08:32,645
That'll be 2,500 baht.

168
00:08:32,646 --> 00:08:34,647
(Shocked)

169
00:08:34,648 --> 00:08:35,681
What, 2,500 baht?

170
00:08:36,216 --> 00:08:38,650
Wait, that's...

171
00:08:38,651 --> 00:08:39,952
That's crazy expensive.

172
00:08:40,121 --> 00:08:41,053
How about 1,000 baht?

173
00:08:41,588 --> 00:08:42,588
Well...

174
00:08:42,589 --> 00:08:43,722
It's way too much.

175
00:08:44,424 --> 00:08:46,859
He said 2,500 baht. What about 1,500 baht?

176
00:08:47,294 --> 00:08:48,628
- Sounds fair.
- You think so?

177
00:08:48,629 --> 00:08:50,296
- That sounds reasonable.
- Should I give it a shot?

178
00:08:50,364 --> 00:08:51,897
Can you do 1,500 baht?

179
00:08:52,199 --> 00:08:53,900
(Negotiating again,
but it's 500 baht over budget.)

180
00:08:54,067 --> 00:08:56,435
(Can we do 1,500 baht instead?)

181
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:59,671
- Okay, 1,500 baht.
- Okay?

182
00:08:59,672 --> 00:09:01,773
Deal? Thank you!

183
00:09:01,774 --> 00:09:05,077
Awesome! Trying out a whole new ride!

184
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:07,913
- Guess I'm pretty good at haggling.
- This looks fun.

185
00:09:09,082 --> 00:09:10,916
(Boarding the songthaew)

186
00:09:12,118 --> 00:09:13,719
They even have fans in here!

187
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:15,755
(Equipped with fans)

188
00:09:16,023 --> 00:09:17,222
Wait, our suitcase!

189
00:09:17,624 --> 00:09:19,425
I almost left our suitcase behind!

190
00:09:19,426 --> 00:09:21,393
I almost forgot it. Thank you!

191
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:22,361
You can leave it up front.

192
00:09:22,495 --> 00:09:24,663
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

193
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,234
Can we open this window?

194
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,902
This one? Probably not.

195
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:31,737
If it gets bumpy, hold on to this.

196
00:09:32,272 --> 00:09:33,873
It gets way bumpier than you'd think.

197
00:09:33,874 --> 00:09:35,708
We can press this when we want to get off.

198
00:09:35,709 --> 00:09:37,743
- Look, they even have this!
- A stop buzzer!

199
00:09:38,264 --> 00:09:39,489
There are USB charging ports too!

200
00:09:39,514 --> 00:09:41,247
- Right here.
- It's surprisingly modern.

201
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:42,147
Very modern.

202
00:09:42,259 --> 00:09:46,086
Can you call a songthaew through an app,
or do you just hail one on the street?

203
00:09:46,087 --> 00:09:48,354
You just flag one down on the street...

204
00:09:48,355 --> 00:09:49,655
and negotiate the fare.

205
00:09:50,224 --> 00:09:52,158
So they just cruise around.

206
00:09:52,159 --> 00:09:53,592
You wave them down and hop on.

207
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,793
It's basically a shared bus.

208
00:09:54,995 --> 00:09:56,895
- We got so lucky today!
- Totally.

209
00:09:56,896 --> 00:09:58,130
(Luckily, they caught one right away)

210
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:00,268
Does that mean
other passengers hop on too?

211
00:10:00,269 --> 00:10:01,934
- Yep.
- Really?

212
00:10:01,935 --> 00:10:03,303
If they're heading in the same direction.

213
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,504
It's like a bus without a fixed route.

214
00:10:05,505 --> 00:10:06,438
Exactly.

215
00:10:07,173 --> 00:10:09,508
- Here we go!
- It's going to get super bumpy.

216
00:10:09,509 --> 00:10:11,643
- Hold on to the rail.
- This is so cool.

217
00:10:11,644 --> 00:10:13,645
It's about an hour's ride, right?

218
00:10:14,115 --> 00:10:16,348
About an hour to an hour and a half.

219
00:10:16,716 --> 00:10:18,617
Won Ji, there are
so many things to do here,

220
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:19,785
like bamboo rafting.

221
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:20,786
Are there a lot of activities around here?

222
00:10:20,787 --> 00:10:22,121
Let's try some!

223
00:10:22,122 --> 00:10:23,689
- Let's do it.
- Sounds good!

224
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,458
Look, this one looks amazing.

225
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:28,827
They even offer
an elephant morning wake-up call!

226
00:10:28,828 --> 00:10:30,028
- An elephant wake-up call?
- An elephant wake-up call?

227
00:10:30,029 --> 00:10:31,597
(Surprised)

228
00:10:31,598 --> 00:10:32,898
"One-hour elephant feeding and walk."

229
00:10:32,899 --> 00:10:34,066
That's awesome!

230
00:10:35,079 --> 00:10:36,712
Look at you, wearing an elephant shirt!

231
00:10:36,737 --> 00:10:39,738
I went full elephant today.
Even my pants have elephants on them.

232
00:10:39,739 --> 00:10:41,273
Even the pants.

233
00:10:41,274 --> 00:10:43,075
My tote bag has elephants too.

234
00:10:43,076 --> 00:10:44,476
(Dressed head-to-toe for elephant day)

235
00:10:44,501 --> 00:10:45,845
I already picked out a name
for an elephant,

236
00:10:45,846 --> 00:10:47,414
and I haven't even met one yet.

237
00:10:47,614 --> 00:10:50,081
- Pupu.
- Pupu?

238
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:51,083
Does that mean "poop"?

239
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:52,051
No!

240
00:10:52,285 --> 00:10:54,553
- It sounds cute.
- You just liked how it sounds?

241
00:10:55,070 --> 00:10:57,456
(Check this out.)

242
00:10:58,392 --> 00:11:00,058
- That looks like so much fun.
- I love being out in nature.

243
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:02,195
"It was an unforgettable experience."

244
00:11:06,309 --> 00:11:07,643
That bump launched us!

245
00:11:07,668 --> 00:11:08,734
It really did.

246
00:11:08,735 --> 00:11:10,178
We got total airtime off our seats.

247
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:11,805
Good thing I used the restroom earlier.

248
00:11:12,539 --> 00:11:14,974
A bump like that will really
get things moving.

249
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:16,575
We'd better hold on tight.

250
00:11:16,576 --> 00:11:20,145
- This feels so dreamy.
- Dreamy.

251
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:22,281
(Sniffs)

252
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:23,483
I can smell the fresh grass.

253
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:25,984
- The grass!
- It smells so fresh.

254
00:11:25,985 --> 00:11:27,586
- So refreshing.
- Totally different vibe.

255
00:11:27,587 --> 00:11:29,154
(Chiang Mai is lush and green.)

256
00:11:29,155 --> 00:11:31,424
Chiang Mai feels completely
different from Bangkok.

257
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:34,226
The sky and the scenery are gorgeous.

258
00:11:34,227 --> 00:11:35,995
- The weather is just incredible.
- It really is.

259
00:11:36,764 --> 00:11:38,664
- It's so nice and breezy.
- Won Ji.

260
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:41,300
Are your glasses giving off
total jungle safari vibes?

261
00:11:41,301 --> 00:11:43,302
- Those look great on you.
- Right?

262
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:46,539
I love how you hype up my glasses
every single time.

263
00:11:46,774 --> 00:11:48,574
You compliment every pair I put on.

264
00:11:48,808 --> 00:11:50,410
Those definitely
have an earthy jungle vibe.

265
00:11:51,571 --> 00:11:52,672
We're flying down the road.

266
00:11:53,079 --> 00:11:53,912
It's really fast.

267
00:11:54,236 --> 00:11:55,730
- It's nice and cool.
- Not hot at all.

268
00:11:55,731 --> 00:11:56,883
Is the breeze helping?

269
00:11:56,884 --> 00:11:57,750
Nice.

270
00:11:57,977 --> 00:12:00,553
We probably have about 30 minutes left.

271
00:12:02,422 --> 00:12:05,258
I must look so hot from over there.

272
00:12:05,824 --> 00:12:06,726
(Impressed)

273
00:12:07,057 --> 00:12:09,729
Showing off her hair extensions.

274
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:11,351
(Suddenly feeling herself)

275
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:13,967
Go flirt with the driver.

276
00:12:14,111 --> 00:12:15,869
You probably look
like a ghost from behind.

277
00:12:16,285 --> 00:12:18,671
There's a ghost right here.

278
00:12:19,772 --> 00:12:22,205
(Lost in the moment, Filming)

279
00:12:22,839 --> 00:12:24,499
(The bewildered introvert)

280
00:12:24,739 --> 00:12:26,779
You look like a Chinese beauty influencer.

281
00:12:27,499 --> 00:12:28,685
(Bursts out laughing)

282
00:12:28,852 --> 00:12:30,717
- A total wanghong.
- Seriously, just like one.

283
00:12:30,999 --> 00:12:32,285
Look up.

284
00:12:32,365 --> 00:12:34,587
A Chinese beauty below,
but someone else up top.

285
00:12:35,032 --> 00:12:37,845
(A wanghong and a ghost)

286
00:12:39,245 --> 00:12:41,094
Nice.

287
00:12:41,185 --> 00:12:42,295
An Asian beauty.

288
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,231
(Another Asian beauty appears.)

289
00:12:46,905 --> 00:12:49,039
<i>Got me looking so crazy right now</i>

290
00:12:50,011 --> 00:12:51,698
(A subtle madness begins.)

291
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:55,642
Nice singing.

292
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:59,856
(The madness spreads.)

293
00:13:00,536 --> 00:13:01,956
(The fascinated introvert)

294
00:13:02,956 --> 00:13:04,010
(I can't back down now.)

295
00:13:04,903 --> 00:13:07,668
(The extroverts are just getting started.)

296
00:13:12,594 --> 00:13:15,041
(Zero energy left)

297
00:13:15,754 --> 00:13:17,452
(Her eyes slowly glaze over.)

298
00:13:17,939 --> 00:13:21,119
(The three extroverts turn
all the way up.)

299
00:13:21,626 --> 00:13:24,106
(The introvert slowly loses her soul.)

300
00:13:24,519 --> 00:13:26,812
(Their energy shows no signs of dropping.)

301
00:13:27,173 --> 00:13:30,077
(This is driving me insane.)

302
00:13:30,357 --> 00:13:31,737
This is the signature move.

303
00:13:31,738 --> 00:13:32,983
- Do it together!
- Really?

304
00:13:33,117 --> 00:13:35,548
Vroom, start the car. That's...

305
00:13:35,603 --> 00:13:38,151
Raise it up!

306
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:39,357
(Jumps up)

307
00:13:39,803 --> 00:13:42,537
(Genuinely aggressive)

308
00:13:43,723 --> 00:13:46,159
(Isn't that way too close to my face?)

309
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,860
That was way too close.

310
00:13:48,623 --> 00:13:51,257
(She finally looks away.)

311
00:13:52,003 --> 00:13:54,210
(Relentless flirting)

312
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:57,603
(Her eyes are starting to water.)

313
00:13:58,183 --> 00:14:00,143
(An introvert's inescapable nightmare)

314
00:14:00,577 --> 00:14:02,490
(When is this going to end?)

315
00:14:03,430 --> 00:14:06,530
(Let me out of here.)

316
00:14:06,963 --> 00:14:10,683
<i>Go higher and higher, fly up high</i>

317
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:11,684
<i>Fly</i>

318
00:14:12,343 --> 00:14:13,286
Fifteen minutes.

319
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,455
Fifteen minutes.

320
00:14:15,537 --> 00:14:18,460
- Look, a convenience store.
- A grocery store too.

321
00:14:18,713 --> 00:14:21,053
It looks just like the valley restaurants
back home.

322
00:14:21,054 --> 00:14:22,695
It does.

323
00:14:23,429 --> 00:14:25,331
- We're here!
- We made it.

324
00:14:25,332 --> 00:14:27,733
Here it is, "Chiang Mai Elephant Friends."

325
00:14:27,757 --> 00:14:28,392
Amazing!

326
00:14:28,393 --> 00:14:29,539
(Arrived at the lodging)

327
00:14:31,392 --> 00:14:33,039
"Chiang Mai Elephant."

328
00:14:34,612 --> 00:14:35,775
Let's go.

329
00:14:36,311 --> 00:14:37,443
Let's hop out.

330
00:14:37,485 --> 00:14:39,379
This is heavy. Help me lift it down.

331
00:14:40,079 --> 00:14:42,015
- It feels so cool here.
- Please grab this.

332
00:14:42,358 --> 00:14:44,831
Okay, that was an awesome ride.

333
00:14:44,878 --> 00:14:45,718
Let's go.

334
00:14:45,743 --> 00:14:48,912
- Let's check in.
- Let's go.

335
00:14:49,276 --> 00:14:52,124
- This is lovely.
- It's so cool.

336
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:55,895
- Hello.
- Hello.

337
00:14:56,296 --> 00:14:58,431
Can we check in now?

338
00:14:58,931 --> 00:15:00,931
Maybe...

339
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,101
- Abra...
- Abra-ca-Empty!

340
00:15:02,287 --> 00:15:03,874
(A goofy dance at check-in)

341
00:15:04,641 --> 00:15:06,261
(Check-in successful)

342
00:15:07,861 --> 00:15:09,925
(Please return the key at check-out.)

343
00:15:09,985 --> 00:15:13,158
(The resort offers elephant experiences.)

344
00:15:13,772 --> 00:15:17,377
(Activity 1: Elephant walking and bathing)

345
00:15:17,378 --> 00:15:19,938
(Activity 2:
Elephant morning wake-up call)

346
00:15:20,258 --> 00:15:23,031
(We're doing both.)

347
00:15:23,056 --> 00:15:24,424
I love it.

348
00:15:25,658 --> 00:15:27,093
- Four people, correct?
- Yes

349
00:15:30,183 --> 00:15:31,443
The total comes to...

350
00:15:31,649 --> 00:15:33,192
It's 9,100 baht total.

351
00:15:33,743 --> 00:15:36,410
- The elephant wake-up call is...
- Wait, wasn't it 900?

352
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:38,175
- Is it really that expensive?
- Nine thousand?

353
00:15:38,538 --> 00:15:42,909
Elephant care for four is 7,600 baht.

354
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:46,612
The elephant wake-up call is 1,500 baht.

355
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:48,147
Who does the wake-up call?

356
00:15:48,263 --> 00:15:49,816
An elephant!

357
00:15:49,856 --> 00:15:50,503
How?

358
00:15:50,527 --> 00:15:52,419
It literally comes to your room
and wakes you up.

359
00:15:53,076 --> 00:15:54,987
It'll even massage your feet.

360
00:15:55,136 --> 00:15:56,155
Seriously?

361
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:58,624
That sounds incredible.

362
00:16:00,176 --> 00:16:03,062
Let's just pay in cash first.

363
00:16:03,429 --> 00:16:05,331
We have basically zero cash left now.

364
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:07,800
We just blew through half of our funds.

365
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:10,563
Good thing we scored
that extra money yesterday.

366
00:16:10,564 --> 00:16:11,571
Seriously.

367
00:16:11,616 --> 00:16:13,906
Dumping our luggage was definitely
the right move.

368
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:17,177
(Payment complete)

369
00:16:18,130 --> 00:16:20,441
Your room is ready, so you can head in.

370
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,814
Okay!

371
00:16:21,935 --> 00:16:23,001
Awesome.

372
00:16:23,002 --> 00:16:24,535
I can't wait to see the room.

373
00:16:24,536 --> 00:16:26,786
Behind you!

374
00:16:27,036 --> 00:16:28,788
Look, elephants!

375
00:16:29,009 --> 00:16:30,123
They're real elephants!

376
00:16:30,849 --> 00:16:33,386
- They're right next to us!
- Incredible.

377
00:16:34,761 --> 00:16:36,496
My dream is finally coming true today.

378
00:16:36,497 --> 00:16:37,353
(Elephants in the distance)

379
00:16:37,533 --> 00:16:39,265
This is unreal.

380
00:16:39,266 --> 00:16:41,266
This is incredible. They're huge!

381
00:16:42,226 --> 00:16:46,547
(Where dense jungle meets
the Mae Wang River)

382
00:16:46,953 --> 00:16:51,373
(Today's stay,
nestled deep in the mountains)

383
00:16:53,340 --> 00:16:55,871
(A special sanctuary surrounded
by elephants and nature)

384
00:16:56,516 --> 00:17:00,958
(A chance to connect up close
with gentle giants)

385
00:17:01,558 --> 00:17:05,664
(A sanctuary providing care
for rescued elephants)

386
00:17:06,244 --> 00:17:09,804
(A special night under the jungle canopy)

387
00:17:10,763 --> 00:17:13,366
- Khop khun chao.
- Khop khun chao.

388
00:17:13,408 --> 00:17:15,408
That's the northern Chiang Mai dialect!

389
00:17:17,501 --> 00:17:20,974
(Heading to the room)

390
00:17:21,307 --> 00:17:22,875
It definitely wasn't cheap.

391
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,777
Well, it goes toward feeding
the elephants.

392
00:17:25,311 --> 00:17:28,981
- It supports the sanctuary.
- It pays for their care.

393
00:17:29,614 --> 00:17:31,451
- How many bags do you have?
- Just one.

394
00:17:31,861 --> 00:17:33,453
We only brought one suitcase.

395
00:17:33,487 --> 00:17:34,481
Perfect.

396
00:17:35,187 --> 00:17:37,924
- Goodness.
- A wooden suspension bridge?

397
00:17:38,554 --> 00:17:39,987
(A signature feature of the resort)

398
00:17:41,094 --> 00:17:43,745
(A suspension bridge connecting
the lobby to the rooms)

399
00:17:43,899 --> 00:17:45,097
All right.

400
00:17:45,539 --> 00:17:46,999
Let's go.

401
00:17:48,639 --> 00:17:51,137
We have to cross this bridge
to get to our room.

402
00:17:51,325 --> 00:17:53,092
Look, it's a rope bridge!

403
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:55,141
I think we need to watch our step.

404
00:17:55,232 --> 00:17:56,846
- Wait.
- This is terrifying.

405
00:17:56,847 --> 00:17:58,511
I'm so bad with heights.

406
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:01,000
(Freaking out
and taking deep breaths first)

407
00:18:01,827 --> 00:18:05,620
(Attempting the bridge again)

408
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,003
This feels a little sketchy.

409
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:09,121
Look straight ahead.

410
00:18:10,103 --> 00:18:10,990
Watch your footing.

411
00:18:12,204 --> 00:18:14,136
- It's swaying so much!
- Look down!

412
00:18:14,137 --> 00:18:15,127
Look at the water!

413
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,064
It's swaying crazy hard.

414
00:18:20,234 --> 00:18:21,401
(Peeking)

415
00:18:21,621 --> 00:18:23,202
Don't look down!

416
00:18:23,287 --> 00:18:24,734
- I'm scared!
- Just don't look down!

417
00:18:24,735 --> 00:18:26,806
(Gaps all over the floorboards)

418
00:18:27,581 --> 00:18:30,079
(Legs trembling)

419
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,844
I really shouldn't have looked down.

420
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:36,115
Look down there. That's awesome!

421
00:18:36,692 --> 00:18:37,817
Hi!

422
00:18:38,065 --> 00:18:40,125
Hello!

423
00:18:40,419 --> 00:18:42,255
- Hello!
- Have a nice day!

424
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:45,925
This place is unbelievable.
It's so gorgeous.

425
00:18:46,592 --> 00:18:48,165
It feels straight out of a fairy tale.

426
00:18:48,190 --> 00:18:49,295
This is magical.

427
00:18:49,296 --> 00:18:50,996
(A fairy-tale world come to life)

428
00:18:52,108 --> 00:18:54,233
We're getting closer to the elephants!

429
00:18:55,007 --> 00:18:57,203
Almost there!

430
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,872
Okay, we made it across!

431
00:19:00,368 --> 00:19:02,174
(Safely made it across the bridge)

432
00:19:02,274 --> 00:19:04,510
Our legs are seriously shaking today.

433
00:19:06,078 --> 00:19:08,247
I definitely didn't expect
a suspension bridge on check-in.

434
00:19:08,248 --> 00:19:09,181
Tell me about it.

435
00:19:09,426 --> 00:19:11,918
They're real elephants!

436
00:19:12,046 --> 00:19:14,046
I've never seen one this close
before in my life!

437
00:19:14,232 --> 00:19:15,221
They're so adorable!

438
00:19:15,472 --> 00:19:17,523
- So cute!
- The one in the middle is adorable!

439
00:19:17,639 --> 00:19:19,759
It's so cute! Look at that skin texture.

440
00:19:19,912 --> 00:19:21,159
(Gasps in excitement)

441
00:19:21,939 --> 00:19:24,959
(Come here, sweetie!)

442
00:19:25,052 --> 00:19:25,992
(Gasps in excitement)

443
00:19:26,019 --> 00:19:27,333
- It's coming over!
- For real?

444
00:19:27,546 --> 00:19:29,702
- Really? Is it coming this way?
- It really is!

445
00:19:29,866 --> 00:19:32,379
- So cute!
- It's walking right toward us!

446
00:19:32,559 --> 00:19:34,440
Nice to meet you!

447
00:19:35,614 --> 00:19:37,649
- Can I touch?
- Yes.

448
00:19:38,058 --> 00:19:39,919
(Seriously?)

449
00:19:41,159 --> 00:19:42,582
It came right up to us!

450
00:19:42,626 --> 00:19:43,749
So sweet!

451
00:19:44,046 --> 00:19:45,685
- Hello.
- Hi!

452
00:19:47,379 --> 00:19:51,299
(The curious elephant walks right over.)

453
00:19:52,325 --> 00:19:53,626
Hello!

454
00:19:53,627 --> 00:19:56,493
(Conducted safely
under professional supervision)

455
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:59,090
Its eyes...
I've never been this close before.

456
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:00,433
It came right up!

457
00:20:00,434 --> 00:20:02,800
(Gently petting the elephant)

458
00:20:03,013 --> 00:20:05,972
Hello.

459
00:20:06,378 --> 00:20:09,548
Hello! This is fascinating.

460
00:20:10,311 --> 00:20:11,377
Hello!

461
00:20:11,557 --> 00:20:13,312
It came so close.

462
00:20:13,313 --> 00:20:14,584
(The bigger they are, the cuter they are.)

463
00:20:14,851 --> 00:20:16,182
Hello!

464
00:20:17,416 --> 00:20:19,185
Wait, I'm actually kind of scared.

465
00:20:19,404 --> 00:20:21,187
I'm scared!

466
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:23,777
Wait, weren't you loving it a second ago?

467
00:20:25,671 --> 00:20:27,824
(Bolts away)

468
00:20:28,744 --> 00:20:31,092
(Running for her life)

469
00:20:31,339 --> 00:20:33,339
What are you doing?

470
00:20:36,145 --> 00:20:38,135
It has way more hair on its head
than I thought.

471
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:39,585
(Total chaos)

472
00:20:39,919 --> 00:20:41,674
Lee Sian is hilarious.

473
00:20:42,433 --> 00:20:43,901
She got spooked.

474
00:20:44,477 --> 00:20:45,499
(Embarrassed)

475
00:20:45,705 --> 00:20:47,912
It's so much bigger up close.

476
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,415
(An intense first encounter
with the elephants)

477
00:20:49,826 --> 00:20:51,020
Unbelievable. I love this.

478
00:20:51,021 --> 00:20:52,618
Look, there's another one up there!

479
00:20:53,106 --> 00:20:54,386
It feels like a storybook.

480
00:20:54,387 --> 00:20:55,688
There's another one!

481
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:02,528
There are so many dogs here too!
This is precious.

482
00:21:02,529 --> 00:21:03,796
This really is paradise.

483
00:21:04,067 --> 00:21:06,532
- Pure paradise.
- Doesn't it feel like a fairy tale?

484
00:21:06,607 --> 00:21:08,367
Imagine living here.

485
00:21:09,552 --> 00:21:11,552
Dogs running around...

486
00:21:11,553 --> 00:21:13,105
and elephants wandering everywhere.

487
00:21:16,519 --> 00:21:18,310
(Almost there)

488
00:21:18,311 --> 00:21:19,506
(10 km)

489
00:21:19,507 --> 00:21:20,846
Wait, 10 kilometers?

490
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:23,003
- You don't mean one kilometer?
- No way.

491
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:24,900
(Just kidding)

492
00:21:25,307 --> 00:21:27,319
- She's hilarious, totally my style.
- She was messing with us.

493
00:21:27,874 --> 00:21:29,422
- Are you holding up okay?
- Yep!

494
00:21:29,647 --> 00:21:32,660
I'm so glad we only brought one suitcase.

495
00:21:32,661 --> 00:21:34,387
Imagine if all four of us
dragged one each...

496
00:21:34,388 --> 00:21:36,388
- One each would've been...
- We'd be dead.

497
00:21:36,389 --> 00:21:37,430
a nightmare.

498
00:21:37,715 --> 00:21:39,565
Good thing we unpacked
and lightened the load yesterday.

499
00:21:41,968 --> 00:21:44,336
Wait, is that our room?
The one way back there?

500
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:47,606
- There's another section.
- Another one?

501
00:21:48,274 --> 00:21:50,274
She did say 10 kilometers earlier.

502
00:21:50,473 --> 00:21:51,277
Wait, what?

503
00:21:51,493 --> 00:21:53,012
We have to walk even further?

504
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:54,112
Just kidding.

505
00:21:55,214 --> 00:21:57,749
Okay, let's go!

506
00:21:57,750 --> 00:21:59,651
(Keep moving.)

507
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,801
So do the elephants actually
come up here...

508
00:22:06,826 --> 00:22:08,060
and wake us up?

509
00:22:08,328 --> 00:22:09,227
Maybe.

510
00:22:10,129 --> 00:22:11,729
Do elephants really roam around here?

511
00:22:12,898 --> 00:22:14,465
I don't see any footprints.

512
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:16,234
Almost there.

513
00:22:16,235 --> 00:22:18,670
- Thank you!
- Two minutes left.

514
00:22:19,372 --> 00:22:20,672
Two minutes!

515
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:21,540
Huh?

516
00:22:21,541 --> 00:22:22,774
What is it?

517
00:22:22,775 --> 00:22:24,976
- Look at that elephant over there.
- An elephant.

518
00:22:24,977 --> 00:22:26,445
(Speaking of elephants)

519
00:22:26,852 --> 00:22:28,453
It's an actual wild elephant.

520
00:22:28,948 --> 00:22:30,381
Are they allowed to hang out here?

521
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:33,718
Those two must be a couple. So cute.

522
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:37,088
I've never seen elephants
in the mountains like this.

523
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:40,291
I guess they just let them free-roam.

524
00:22:40,292 --> 00:22:41,727
I want to take one home with me.

525
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:44,762
- Their faces are so adorable.
- Right?

526
00:22:45,832 --> 00:22:47,799
Let's keep going. Bye.

527
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:48,966
Bye-bye!

528
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:49,834
See you later.

529
00:22:49,835 --> 00:22:51,369
So elephants really do come
all the way up here.

530
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:53,738
- They probably make it up to our lodge.
- To wake us up?

531
00:22:53,739 --> 00:22:55,139
That is so cool.

532
00:22:56,409 --> 00:22:57,175
This is so much fun!

533
00:22:57,576 --> 00:22:59,210
(Picks up something from the ground)

534
00:23:01,381 --> 00:23:02,280
It's one of those!

535
00:23:02,281 --> 00:23:03,948
- What is it?
- That!

536
00:23:03,949 --> 00:23:05,149
You know...

537
00:23:05,351 --> 00:23:06,818
Remember roly-polies
from when we were kids?

538
00:23:06,819 --> 00:23:08,286
It's a giant roly-poly!

539
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:09,454
A giant pill bug!

540
00:23:12,291 --> 00:23:13,291
It's uncurling!

541
00:23:13,292 --> 00:23:14,859
(Pill bug slowly unfurling)

542
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:16,694
So that's what it looks like.

543
00:23:17,263 --> 00:23:19,697
Curl up! Roll into a ball!

544
00:23:22,702 --> 00:23:24,403
You're one impressive little bug,
aren't you?

545
00:23:24,404 --> 00:23:25,479
It rolled into a ball again.

546
00:23:25,504 --> 00:23:27,772
Now it's uncurling.

547
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:29,841
Roll up again!

548
00:23:31,711 --> 00:23:33,679
Sorry.

549
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,947
There are so many
fascinating things in nature.

550
00:23:35,948 --> 00:23:36,882
Oh my gosh.

551
00:23:37,350 --> 00:23:39,484
I've been to Chiang Mai five times,

552
00:23:39,485 --> 00:23:41,353
but I never knew a place
like this existed.

553
00:23:41,687 --> 00:23:44,088
It's so cool that you can just
casually bump into elephants.

554
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,123
This is unbelievable.

555
00:23:45,891 --> 00:23:48,093
- Are we almost there?
- I see something up ahead.

556
00:23:51,864 --> 00:23:53,231
This is insane!

557
00:23:54,366 --> 00:23:56,267
This is literal paradise.

558
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:57,168
Is this our place?

559
00:23:57,169 --> 00:23:59,337
This place is gorgeous.

560
00:23:59,338 --> 00:24:00,671
Look at this view.

561
00:24:00,672 --> 00:24:02,206
Incredible!

562
00:24:03,008 --> 00:24:05,910
(Surrounded by a lush, green forest)

563
00:24:07,046 --> 00:24:10,882
(A private cabin
just for the four of them)

564
00:24:14,653 --> 00:24:16,721
This place is breathtakingly beautiful.

565
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:20,057
This is amazing.

566
00:24:21,527 --> 00:24:23,795
I feel like I can touch the clouds.

567
00:24:25,298 --> 00:24:26,732
Look, there's even a swing!

568
00:24:27,066 --> 00:24:27,999
This is wild.

569
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:30,568
It's so nice and cool.

570
00:24:30,771 --> 00:24:32,637
Totally.

571
00:24:33,072 --> 00:24:35,473
- It's so breezy.
- So cool.

572
00:24:35,808 --> 00:24:38,243
- We made it.
- We did.

573
00:24:38,611 --> 00:24:40,645
I'm obsessed with this place.

574
00:24:45,050 --> 00:24:49,754
(Their lodge for the day)

575
00:24:50,589 --> 00:24:53,190
(Sharing one room together)

576
00:24:53,359 --> 00:24:55,294
There's even a patio terrace!

577
00:24:55,295 --> 00:24:57,729
The weather is so nice and cool.

578
00:24:58,697 --> 00:25:00,097
This place is gorgeous.

579
00:25:02,635 --> 00:25:03,602
It's unbelievable.

580
00:25:04,236 --> 00:25:07,605
Let's just sit out here
and listen to nature.

581
00:25:07,774 --> 00:25:11,309
It's so breezy and refreshing.

582
00:25:12,211 --> 00:25:14,747
Just chilling and doing nothing
sounds amazing right now.

583
00:25:15,613 --> 00:25:18,316
I'm so glad the weather is nice.

584
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:20,951
- Should we change first?
- Sounds good.

585
00:25:21,921 --> 00:25:23,622
Let's drop our bags and grab some food.

586
00:25:23,623 --> 00:25:24,956
- Sounds good!
- Yes!

587
00:25:24,957 --> 00:25:26,157
Okay.

588
00:25:26,859 --> 00:25:27,926
I'm starving.

589
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:30,061
Me too!

590
00:25:30,629 --> 00:25:33,331
We're true jungle adventurers today!

591
00:25:33,332 --> 00:25:36,267
(Singing)

592
00:25:36,268 --> 00:25:38,169
Mr. Elephant,

593
00:25:38,704 --> 00:25:40,905
why is your nose so long?

594
00:25:40,906 --> 00:25:42,607
Why the long nose?

595
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:45,910
This must be the restaurant!

596
00:25:46,312 --> 00:25:47,879
Oh, yeah!

597
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,214
(Restaurant)

598
00:25:49,949 --> 00:25:51,549
I see an elephant over there.

599
00:25:52,484 --> 00:25:55,019
Do you think we can watch them
while we eat?

600
00:25:55,020 --> 00:25:56,053
That's amazing!

601
00:25:56,455 --> 00:25:58,289
- Hello.
- Look, a doggy.

602
00:25:58,691 --> 00:26:01,325
Hi there!

603
00:26:01,326 --> 00:26:04,028
Were you taking a nap?

604
00:26:04,230 --> 00:26:05,764
He wants me to leave him alone.

605
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:08,400
Look, there's a cat too!

606
00:26:08,401 --> 00:26:09,700
This place is heaven.

607
00:26:09,870 --> 00:26:11,836
Absolute paradise.

608
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:15,440
It feels like a spot where you should
order boiled chicken soup.

609
00:26:15,441 --> 00:26:16,941
It's so fancy here.

610
00:26:17,676 --> 00:26:19,744
- And so breezy.
- It is.

611
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:21,012
Look at the seating inside.

612
00:26:21,013 --> 00:26:22,947
This place is lovely.

613
00:26:23,449 --> 00:26:25,784
We're literally surrounded by nature.

614
00:26:26,452 --> 00:26:28,186
It looks like a fairy-tale cottage.

615
00:26:28,187 --> 00:26:30,055
It's paradise.

616
00:26:30,389 --> 00:26:31,956
Let's sit over here.

617
00:26:31,957 --> 00:26:34,058
- Okay!
- Sure.

618
00:26:34,761 --> 00:26:36,494
This place is seriously nice.

619
00:26:36,762 --> 00:26:40,565
It feels so refreshing
eating right next to the river.

620
00:26:40,866 --> 00:26:42,200
This whole place feels like a fairy tale,

621
00:26:42,201 --> 00:26:43,601
with the elephants and everything.

622
00:26:43,869 --> 00:26:45,536
Everyone working here looks so happy too.

623
00:26:45,537 --> 00:26:46,571
The staff?

624
00:26:46,572 --> 00:26:49,640
- They look so joyful.
- Peak job satisfaction.

625
00:26:49,808 --> 00:26:51,475
You look pretty satisfied yourself.

626
00:26:51,476 --> 00:26:52,510
Totally.

627
00:26:52,978 --> 00:26:54,445
- You caught me.
- I caught you.

628
00:26:55,372 --> 00:26:56,214
Is something here?

629
00:26:56,215 --> 00:26:58,183
- Hello!
- Hi!

630
00:26:58,184 --> 00:27:00,585
We definitely have to try
the bamboo rafting!

631
00:27:01,220 --> 00:27:03,221
This looks like the boarding dock.

632
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,357
They're pulling up.

633
00:27:07,493 --> 00:27:09,761
That looks like so much fun.

634
00:27:11,397 --> 00:27:13,465
Is this what true peace feels like?

635
00:27:15,667 --> 00:27:17,001
Hi!

636
00:27:17,436 --> 00:27:18,569
Hello!

637
00:27:19,705 --> 00:27:21,507
The river looks
just like a milk tea latte.

638
00:27:21,934 --> 00:27:23,501
- That actually sounds delicious.
- Delicious.

639
00:27:24,409 --> 00:27:25,945
I kind of want to ask
if they have chai tea.

640
00:27:25,946 --> 00:27:27,746
Yeah, it totally looks like a chai latte.

641
00:27:28,847 --> 00:27:29,713
There's the menu!

642
00:27:29,714 --> 00:27:31,982
Let's check out the menu.

643
00:27:33,352 --> 00:27:35,019
Everything looks delicious.

644
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:36,654
Look, morning glory!

645
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,323
Let's look over the whole menu first.

646
00:27:38,324 --> 00:27:39,824
There's tom yum goong!

647
00:27:40,326 --> 00:27:42,694
Let's order two dishes each
since we worked hard today.

648
00:27:43,339 --> 00:27:45,774
(We're ready to order.)

649
00:27:45,799 --> 00:27:47,432
We earned it!

650
00:27:47,433 --> 00:27:49,234
One tom yum goong,

651
00:27:49,436 --> 00:27:50,768
two pad thais,

652
00:27:51,070 --> 00:27:52,570
one mushroom dish...

653
00:27:52,871 --> 00:27:54,705
One of this one.

654
00:27:54,916 --> 00:27:57,084
- One morning glory.
- Morning glory.

655
00:27:57,109 --> 00:27:58,442
Are you getting fried rice?

656
00:27:58,443 --> 00:28:00,478
One fried rice, please.

657
00:28:00,612 --> 00:28:01,545
Thank you!

658
00:28:01,546 --> 00:28:03,581
(Order complete)

659
00:28:05,184 --> 00:28:06,351
(Singing)

660
00:28:06,352 --> 00:28:08,052
I went full elephant-core today.

661
00:28:08,053 --> 00:28:11,055
Though I think real elephants
are way cuter.

662
00:28:11,490 --> 00:28:12,446
What do you mean?

663
00:28:12,470 --> 00:28:14,026
You were literally running away
from one earlier.

664
00:28:14,426 --> 00:28:16,060
First off,

665
00:28:16,395 --> 00:28:18,397
their skin was a lot rougher
than I expected.

666
00:28:18,398 --> 00:28:19,430
True.

667
00:28:19,431 --> 00:28:21,432
And they're so bristly!

668
00:28:21,433 --> 00:28:22,533
They have so much hair.

669
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:25,236
- Especially around their mouths.
- Like a scrub brush!

670
00:28:25,237 --> 00:28:26,038
Exactly.

671
00:28:26,390 --> 00:28:27,438
In patches.

672
00:28:27,439 --> 00:28:31,008
- I thought they'd feel smoother.
- Like the cute drawing on your shirt!

673
00:28:31,009 --> 00:28:32,176
Doesn't it look smooth?

674
00:28:32,177 --> 00:28:33,344
Totally.

675
00:28:33,612 --> 00:28:34,912
(Laughs)

676
00:28:34,913 --> 00:28:36,213
Something is coming!

677
00:28:37,575 --> 00:28:39,961
(The food starts to appear.)

678
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,320
Mushrooms.

679
00:28:42,688 --> 00:28:44,489
I've been dying to try these.

680
00:28:44,490 --> 00:28:45,724
I love this dish so much.

681
00:28:45,725 --> 00:28:47,558
Morning glory!

682
00:28:48,127 --> 00:28:48,993
Thank you.

683
00:28:48,994 --> 00:28:50,828
The pad thai looks amazing too.

684
00:28:52,097 --> 00:28:54,398
Let's dig in!

685
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:55,966
Enjoy the meal!

686
00:28:58,670 --> 00:29:00,004
(Nom)

687
00:29:00,005 --> 00:29:01,507
It's piping hot and so delicious.

688
00:29:01,774 --> 00:29:02,707
This is so good.

689
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,009
(Munch)

690
00:29:05,010 --> 00:29:06,177
It's good!

691
00:29:06,178 --> 00:29:07,411
It's delicious, right?

692
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,979
(Yum!)

693
00:29:09,948 --> 00:29:11,216
Do you want some tom yum goong?

694
00:29:11,316 --> 00:29:13,550
- Thank you, Won Ji!
- Thank you.

695
00:29:15,621 --> 00:29:17,755
(Brimming)

696
00:29:18,690 --> 00:29:20,391
(Serving up the tom yum goong)

697
00:29:21,727 --> 00:29:23,628
- Won Ji, this is so good.
- I know, right?

698
00:29:24,063 --> 00:29:25,330
This place is amazing.

699
00:29:26,398 --> 00:29:27,898
It's spicy and so satisfying.

700
00:29:27,899 --> 00:29:29,033
Total soul food.

701
00:29:30,469 --> 00:29:32,403
It tastes even better
after sweating it out.

702
00:29:32,838 --> 00:29:33,871
This spot is wonderful.

703
00:29:33,872 --> 00:29:34,872
(Extremely satisfied)

704
00:29:34,873 --> 00:29:35,706
Right.

705
00:29:36,142 --> 00:29:39,377
This reminds me
of that giraffe manor in Kenya.

706
00:29:39,478 --> 00:29:40,978
I know that place!

707
00:29:40,979 --> 00:29:41,946
I saw the video!

708
00:29:41,947 --> 00:29:45,049
The giraffes stick their heads
right through the windows.

709
00:29:45,050 --> 00:29:48,186
And you get to feed them breakfast.

710
00:29:48,287 --> 00:29:51,422
They stroll over
through the morning mist at dawn.

711
00:29:51,723 --> 00:29:53,057
That sounds magical.

712
00:29:53,082 --> 00:29:53,958
It was so much fun,

713
00:29:53,982 --> 00:29:55,550
and this place has that same vibe,
I guess.

714
00:29:56,028 --> 00:29:58,463
I can't wait to feed the elephants.

715
00:29:58,964 --> 00:30:00,599
They grab the food
with their trunks like this.

716
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,666
Elephants actually intimidate me a little.

717
00:30:02,667 --> 00:30:04,702
But they're incredibly smart.

718
00:30:04,870 --> 00:30:07,205
Some elephants can paint.

719
00:30:07,766 --> 00:30:09,075
They hold the brush with their trunks.

720
00:30:09,107 --> 00:30:11,109
- People even buy them.
- Really?

721
00:30:11,376 --> 00:30:13,410
Their intelligence is on par
with human toddlers.

722
00:30:13,411 --> 00:30:14,845
Seriously?

723
00:30:14,870 --> 00:30:16,790
Then we might actually be able
to communicate with them!

724
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:17,748
(Chuckle)

725
00:30:18,117 --> 00:30:20,185
Speaking of which,

726
00:30:20,385 --> 00:30:22,119
I realized Gabee watched
so many of my videos.

727
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,153
I really did!

728
00:30:23,154 --> 00:30:25,289
- I even watched all your latest ones.
- She's a huge fan.

729
00:30:25,290 --> 00:30:26,890
Won Ji, I'm such a big fan of yours.

730
00:30:26,891 --> 00:30:29,927
I always wanted to do
"World Dice Tour" with you!

731
00:30:30,262 --> 00:30:31,495
You teamed up with Kwaktube.

732
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:33,131
That was so fun!

733
00:30:33,132 --> 00:30:35,466
(I loved it in its own way.)

734
00:30:35,801 --> 00:30:37,635
That's why I'm loving this trip so much.

735
00:30:37,837 --> 00:30:38,769
I love it.

736
00:30:38,937 --> 00:30:41,605
I'm a little shy,
so I might be awkward at showing it.

737
00:30:41,606 --> 00:30:43,474
- No, I can totally feel the love.
- Can you?

738
00:30:43,475 --> 00:30:45,509
- You can feel it?
- Absolutely!

739
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:46,610
I'm waiting.

740
00:30:46,747 --> 00:30:48,051
(Making eyes)

741
00:30:48,214 --> 00:30:49,948
I love you so much!

742
00:30:50,182 --> 00:30:51,182
(Blushing)

743
00:30:51,183 --> 00:30:52,750
We're all each other's biggest fans.

744
00:30:52,751 --> 00:30:54,219
I'm a huge fan of Gabee.

745
00:30:55,087 --> 00:30:57,221
And I've watched
everything Sian was in too.

746
00:30:57,589 --> 00:30:58,822
Every single thing?

747
00:30:58,823 --> 00:31:00,791
Every single thing!

748
00:31:00,792 --> 00:31:02,526
Ever since I was little.

749
00:31:02,661 --> 00:31:04,395
Really?

750
00:31:04,396 --> 00:31:07,264
And I watched Harimu back on "Cap-Teen."

751
00:31:07,265 --> 00:31:08,666
"Cap-Teen"? Oh my gosh!

752
00:31:08,667 --> 00:31:10,868
- You know "Cap-Teen?"
- Yeah.

753
00:31:11,069 --> 00:31:13,037
Harimu made such a strong impression.

754
00:31:13,405 --> 00:31:15,239
Right from the start,
she had crazy charisma.

755
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,841
She just stood out.

756
00:31:16,842 --> 00:31:18,509
Didn't you rap back then too?

757
00:31:18,510 --> 00:31:19,410
Yes!

758
00:31:19,411 --> 00:31:21,278
There weren't any dance survival shows
back then,

759
00:31:21,279 --> 00:31:23,647
so I took whatever opportunity
I could just to perform.

760
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:25,083
- Right.
- That's amazing.

761
00:31:25,084 --> 00:31:26,851
I had to get it out of my system.

762
00:31:26,876 --> 00:31:29,578
Back then, I was spitting bars like this.

763
00:31:30,956 --> 00:31:32,390
She's so multi-talented.

764
00:31:32,859 --> 00:31:33,792
As for me,

765
00:31:33,817 --> 00:31:35,894
I've been taking Gabee's dance classes
since I was little.

766
00:31:35,895 --> 00:31:36,761
Oh, that's right.

767
00:31:36,762 --> 00:31:38,162
(Reenacting her younger self
in Gabee's class)

768
00:31:38,163 --> 00:31:39,497
Oh my gosh.

769
00:31:40,732 --> 00:31:42,866
That was my very first heels class!

770
00:31:42,867 --> 00:31:43,600
I remember.

771
00:31:44,002 --> 00:31:45,436
Back then, Gabee told me...

772
00:31:45,437 --> 00:31:47,538
that this class was
the express ticket to LA.

773
00:31:47,563 --> 00:31:49,430
Right, I did say that.

774
00:31:51,782 --> 00:31:53,995
- Oh, my gosh! You remember that?
- Yeah!

775
00:31:53,996 --> 00:31:57,182
I was instructing a dancing class
back then.

776
00:31:57,236 --> 00:32:01,219
I was probably in middle school...

777
00:32:01,410 --> 00:32:02,554
when I attended your class.

778
00:32:04,429 --> 00:32:05,881
I see.

779
00:32:06,425 --> 00:32:08,293
This is insane!

780
00:32:08,294 --> 00:32:09,454
What's happening?

781
00:32:09,455 --> 00:32:12,964
This is so giving girls' day vibes.

782
00:32:14,089 --> 00:32:15,562
Not girls' night.

783
00:32:16,635 --> 00:32:18,635
So we were all keeping an eye
on each other.

784
00:32:18,636 --> 00:32:20,972
What are the chances
we'd meet again like this?

785
00:32:20,974 --> 00:32:21,976
- It's so wild.
- Honestly amazing.

786
00:32:22,168 --> 00:32:25,010
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

787
00:32:25,637 --> 00:32:26,678
Our little money manager!

788
00:32:27,007 --> 00:32:31,286
It's 93... I mean, 930.

789
00:32:31,519 --> 00:32:35,692
(Fueled up and ready for the elephants)

790
00:32:35,872 --> 00:32:38,477
- Ellie!
- Ellie!

791
00:32:38,524 --> 00:32:40,546
- Yeah!
- We got to get the Ellie!

792
00:32:40,566 --> 00:32:43,095
Wow, elephant booty!

793
00:32:44,177 --> 00:32:47,303
- Elephant booty!
- Wow!

794
00:32:53,494 --> 00:32:58,788
(Three elephants are
already waiting for them.)

795
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:01,813
Gosh, this is crazy!

796
00:33:01,914 --> 00:33:03,482
There's grass growing on it!

797
00:33:04,926 --> 00:33:07,166
Come closer.

798
00:33:07,832 --> 00:33:11,026
(Politely greeting them first)

799
00:33:12,066 --> 00:33:15,146
(The elephants calmly welcome them.)

800
00:33:15,147 --> 00:33:16,862
Your patterns are so pretty!

801
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:19,231
- Can I touch them?
- Yes, you can. Come loser.

802
00:33:20,793 --> 00:33:22,720
(As they try to gently communicate,)

803
00:33:23,244 --> 00:33:24,603
- Hi, sweety.
- Hello.

804
00:33:24,604 --> 00:33:26,920
(the elephants are slowly
approaching them.)

805
00:33:27,473 --> 00:33:29,641
- Call her Sa Tung.
- Sa Tung.

806
00:33:29,667 --> 00:33:30,876
- Sa Tung.
- She is Grandma.

807
00:33:31,033 --> 00:33:33,278
- Grandma!
- She's 48 years old.

808
00:33:33,279 --> 00:33:34,719
- She's 40 years old?
- Yes, 48.

809
00:33:34,720 --> 00:33:36,314
She's 48 years old!

810
00:33:36,315 --> 00:33:38,165
(Sa Tung is the biggest grandma elephant.)

811
00:33:38,166 --> 00:33:39,584
She's pretty old.

812
00:33:39,585 --> 00:33:40,619
How fascinating.

813
00:33:41,399 --> 00:33:42,788
This one's a baby!

814
00:33:43,878 --> 00:33:46,158
- Five years old.
- So cute!

815
00:33:46,159 --> 00:33:47,492
She keeps moving her trunk like this.

816
00:33:48,019 --> 00:33:49,728
Even her eyelashes are beautiful.

817
00:33:50,385 --> 00:33:52,385
This one is the grandmother. She's 48.

818
00:33:52,386 --> 00:33:54,331
(While everyone is busy watching)

819
00:33:55,467 --> 00:33:58,205
(Standing awkwardly)

820
00:33:58,985 --> 00:34:01,339
How are you all not scared?

821
00:34:02,249 --> 00:34:03,562
(Sian can't even touch them.)

822
00:34:03,563 --> 00:34:04,802
(Startled)

823
00:34:05,309 --> 00:34:06,211
(Terrified)

824
00:34:06,212 --> 00:34:07,078
You good?

825
00:34:07,079 --> 00:34:08,647
You're their fan, aren't you?

826
00:34:08,648 --> 00:34:09,915
I am.

827
00:34:09,952 --> 00:34:10,949
Weren't you their fan?

828
00:34:10,950 --> 00:34:13,118
But it has too much hair.
I wasn't expecting that.

829
00:34:15,366 --> 00:34:17,122
You said you like them.

830
00:34:17,123 --> 00:34:18,443
(Easier said than touched.)

831
00:34:20,219 --> 00:34:21,359
What's wrong with you?

832
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:23,092
(She's the one who touched it first!)

833
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:25,464
- Hi, Grandma!
- She's grandma Sa Tung.

834
00:34:25,797 --> 00:34:27,232
You look so young!

835
00:34:28,763 --> 00:34:30,936
- Grandma doesn't have a lot of hair.
- You're right.

836
00:34:32,090 --> 00:34:35,083
Grandma has dotted patterns.

837
00:34:35,390 --> 00:34:38,169
What are you doing?
You don't have to touch them.

838
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:40,212
But I really want to touch her!

839
00:34:40,310 --> 00:34:41,723
Just a bit slowly.

840
00:34:41,724 --> 00:34:43,281
Slowly approach her.

841
00:34:43,330 --> 00:34:46,551
She's a 48-year-old grandma. Say hello.

842
00:34:46,557 --> 00:34:47,219
Well done.

843
00:34:47,220 --> 00:34:47,986
You're good.

844
00:34:48,490 --> 00:34:49,921
Hello.

845
00:34:49,922 --> 00:34:51,764
(Flinching at every glance)

846
00:34:51,924 --> 00:34:54,659
Hello. You're so pretty. Thank you.

847
00:34:54,660 --> 00:34:56,707
- Okay, I'm going to go for it.
- She's so funny.

848
00:34:56,708 --> 00:34:58,020
(Gabee inspires a little courage.)

849
00:34:58,926 --> 00:34:59,865
Yes, just like that.

850
00:35:00,732 --> 00:35:02,732
Are you enjoying it, or not?

851
00:35:03,808 --> 00:35:06,815
(A fierce battle between fangirling
and survival instincts)

852
00:35:07,328 --> 00:35:09,040
There's one more.

853
00:35:09,062 --> 00:35:11,209
- Chai Lai.
- Chai Lai!

854
00:35:12,282 --> 00:35:15,382
(13-year-old female elephant, "Chai Lai")

855
00:35:15,383 --> 00:35:17,516
- Chai Lai means beautiful.
- Beautiful!

856
00:35:17,710 --> 00:35:19,818
Chai Lai means beautiful, he says.

857
00:35:19,896 --> 00:35:21,386
Wow, look at her eyes!

858
00:35:22,087 --> 00:35:23,421
It's so big!

859
00:35:24,103 --> 00:35:25,190
She's huge.

860
00:35:25,191 --> 00:35:26,836
- It's big, yeah?
- Yes!

861
00:35:26,911 --> 00:35:27,726
So big.

862
00:35:27,727 --> 00:35:29,261
She weighs 3,000kg.

863
00:35:29,864 --> 00:35:31,897
She's 3,000kg!

864
00:35:33,144 --> 00:35:34,900
Are they sensitive?

865
00:35:35,021 --> 00:35:37,981
They're not. You can touch them.

866
00:35:40,547 --> 00:35:43,661
(A baby trunk offered for a handshake.)

867
00:35:43,907 --> 00:35:46,778
Why are you so scared of them?

868
00:35:47,200 --> 00:35:49,653
- Hey, there!
- And how come you're so good at this?

869
00:35:49,654 --> 00:35:52,050
- Didn't you just meet her today?
- Yes. You should try to touch her.

870
00:35:52,051 --> 00:35:53,204
(Challenge accepted)

871
00:35:53,850 --> 00:35:54,980
(One-woman chaos)

872
00:35:54,981 --> 00:35:56,870
She's hilarious.

873
00:35:56,971 --> 00:35:58,623
Look at her!

874
00:35:58,818 --> 00:36:00,458
She's pure comedy!

875
00:36:01,251 --> 00:36:02,164
(Flick)

876
00:36:02,165 --> 00:36:03,762
Touch it, or leave it! Make up your mind.

877
00:36:04,384 --> 00:36:06,031
Just put your hand out like this.

878
00:36:10,658 --> 00:36:14,073
(A handshake turns into a talent show.)

879
00:36:14,119 --> 00:36:16,128
Hello, mother.

880
00:36:16,129 --> 00:36:18,577
(Someone greets
like they meet a mother-in-law,)

881
00:36:19,033 --> 00:36:21,646
(and someone takes selfies together.)

882
00:36:21,913 --> 00:36:24,149
- I can feel the sweat.
- Right?

883
00:36:24,150 --> 00:36:25,903
(But Sian can barely touch her trunk.)

884
00:36:26,070 --> 00:36:28,935
(A scaredy-cat with impeccable manners )

885
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:30,288
I'm so sorry.

886
00:36:31,125 --> 00:36:35,783
For now, let's go up there
and hang out with them.

887
00:36:35,803 --> 00:36:36,962
Perfect! I love it!

888
00:36:37,103 --> 00:36:40,810
- We'll walk and bathe them at the river.
- So cute.

889
00:36:41,066 --> 00:36:43,066
- Okay.
- Okay, let's go!

890
00:36:43,067 --> 00:36:44,202
Come on.

891
00:36:44,973 --> 00:36:46,071
You come with us too!

892
00:36:47,753 --> 00:36:52,293
(A beautiful path
surrounded by lush greenery)

893
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:53,511
They're so cute.

894
00:36:53,845 --> 00:36:55,113
Come on!

895
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:59,050
This is seriously insane.

896
00:36:59,317 --> 00:37:01,032
We're taking a stroll with an elephant!

897
00:37:01,033 --> 00:37:02,387
This is amazing.

898
00:37:02,388 --> 00:37:03,922
Alright. Sian can touch her now.

899
00:37:05,426 --> 00:37:07,440
(Sian is feeling a little braver.)

900
00:37:08,326 --> 00:37:09,961
This is fascinating.

901
00:37:10,795 --> 00:37:12,497
It's like we're in a fairytale.

902
00:37:12,812 --> 00:37:13,798
It's so amazing.

903
00:37:13,926 --> 00:37:15,500
A real-life elephant!

904
00:37:16,001 --> 00:37:17,259
It feels like a dream.

905
00:37:18,332 --> 00:37:20,838
I never thought
we'd get to see one this close.

906
00:37:20,839 --> 00:37:22,764
(The kind of dream you have
after falling asleep to "The Lion King")

907
00:37:23,050 --> 00:37:25,143
- They're hungry.
- Hungry?

908
00:37:25,144 --> 00:37:27,770
- They want to eat.
- Okay. Let's eat.

909
00:37:27,957 --> 00:37:30,348
Do they understand what he's saying?

910
00:37:30,815 --> 00:37:32,530
- I guess they do.
- That's crazy.

911
00:37:32,730 --> 00:37:34,488
I can't believe we're walking with them.

912
00:37:34,489 --> 00:37:35,987
This is so cool.

913
00:37:37,455 --> 00:37:39,257
- Where do they eat?
- I wonder.

914
00:37:39,328 --> 00:37:40,910
Looks like they have a restaurant
they go to!

915
00:37:40,911 --> 00:37:41,638
I guess so.

916
00:37:42,127 --> 00:37:44,229
It must be their favorite restaurant!

917
00:37:44,753 --> 00:37:46,998
- I can't get over the grass on its back!
- I know, right?

918
00:37:46,999 --> 00:37:48,600
- It's like a cartoon.
- It grew on it, right?

919
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:53,471
Is that grass actually growing
on its back?

920
00:37:53,793 --> 00:37:56,441
- They put it there for fun.
- They did it themselves. I see.

921
00:37:57,119 --> 00:37:59,866
It acts like a mosquito repellent.

922
00:37:59,906 --> 00:38:02,480
- I guess it keeps the mosquitoes away.
- It looks cute on it.

923
00:38:03,348 --> 00:38:07,688
- Now we'll feed them here, okay?
- Okay!

924
00:38:08,161 --> 00:38:10,145
- What will they be eating?
- Is that their snack?

925
00:38:10,145 --> 00:38:11,039
It's sugarcane!

926
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:12,616
(Today's menu: Sugarcane)

927
00:38:12,688 --> 00:38:14,068
They love it!

928
00:38:14,069 --> 00:38:16,094
(They're already lining up.)

929
00:38:16,448 --> 00:38:18,368
They eat 250kg.

930
00:38:19,081 --> 00:38:20,523
- Per day?
- Yes, per day.

931
00:38:20,524 --> 00:38:22,143
They can't wait to eat. For one, 250kg.

932
00:38:22,867 --> 00:38:24,736
How many times do they poop?

933
00:38:25,367 --> 00:38:26,671
- Anytime they want.
- Anytime!

934
00:38:26,672 --> 00:38:28,773
Really? I can't wait!

935
00:38:29,194 --> 00:38:30,927
Take some sugarcane.

936
00:38:31,381 --> 00:38:34,388
- Take two or three, okay?
- Okay.

937
00:38:35,134 --> 00:38:36,740
(Trunk immediately reaching for it)

938
00:38:36,741 --> 00:38:37,934
(Snatch)

939
00:38:38,101 --> 00:38:40,618
Wow! You're so amazing!

940
00:38:40,772 --> 00:38:42,654
<i>- Mr. Elephant uses his trunk as his hand!
- Mr. Elephant uses his trunk as his hand!</i>

941
00:38:42,732 --> 00:38:45,557
<i>He eats his snacks with his trunk!</i>

942
00:38:46,159 --> 00:38:48,545
(Gabee gives one to the baby elephant.)

943
00:38:49,165 --> 00:38:52,766
(She takes two and only eats one.)

944
00:38:53,386 --> 00:38:55,700
You use your trunk like a pro!

945
00:38:55,872 --> 00:38:57,535
Wow, it's over there.

946
00:38:57,952 --> 00:39:00,106
(This time,
the baby elephant goes to Sian.)

947
00:39:00,537 --> 00:39:02,272
Look at that.

948
00:39:02,477 --> 00:39:03,641
- Wow.
- Awesome.

949
00:39:03,642 --> 00:39:04,910
(Eek!)

950
00:39:05,344 --> 00:39:07,750
(Not quite besties yet.)

951
00:39:08,077 --> 00:39:10,849
This way. Alright!

952
00:39:10,850 --> 00:39:13,463
They're very hungry and happy.

953
00:39:13,636 --> 00:39:15,053
This is so interesting!

954
00:39:15,054 --> 00:39:16,888
You already have one!

955
00:39:17,094 --> 00:39:18,757
- You have one.
- Eat yours first.

956
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:19,780
Yes, eat it first.

957
00:39:19,781 --> 00:39:21,060
- I think she understands what I'm saying.
- Good girl!

958
00:39:21,061 --> 00:39:22,360
- Well done.
- She understands.

959
00:39:23,267 --> 00:39:25,930
Come this way.

960
00:39:25,931 --> 00:39:28,580
(They move to a wider place.)

961
00:39:28,647 --> 00:39:31,703
- This place is huge!
- It's surreal.

962
00:39:32,737 --> 00:39:34,539
(Sneak)

963
00:39:34,540 --> 00:39:35,760
She tried to open it.

964
00:39:35,761 --> 00:39:37,761
- I think she can do it.
- Right?

965
00:39:37,762 --> 00:39:40,111
It's beyond cute.

966
00:39:40,112 --> 00:39:41,746
(Shaking tail)

967
00:39:41,817 --> 00:39:43,248
This feels like a fairytale.

968
00:39:43,249 --> 00:39:45,084
(She instantly copies
the tail-swing move.)

969
00:39:45,657 --> 00:39:46,518
Come here.

970
00:39:47,519 --> 00:39:49,287
Grab it like this. Wow!

971
00:39:49,824 --> 00:39:52,056
Your trunk really is your hand, isn't it?

972
00:39:52,157 --> 00:39:53,258
Yes!

973
00:39:53,904 --> 00:39:56,456
(Sian is still struggling
with the baby elephant.)

974
00:39:56,457 --> 00:39:58,557
(Flinch)

975
00:39:59,224 --> 00:40:00,165
I'm still scared.

976
00:40:00,166 --> 00:40:01,132
Okay.

977
00:40:01,370 --> 00:40:04,169
Shake your trunk slowly!
You're going to make me jump.

978
00:40:04,435 --> 00:40:05,703
Slowly!

979
00:40:06,377 --> 00:40:07,972
So cute.

980
00:40:07,973 --> 00:40:10,137
(She takes it, then fakes eating it!)

981
00:40:10,724 --> 00:40:12,010
Hey, what are you doing?

982
00:40:13,131 --> 00:40:14,579
Look at her control her trunk.

983
00:40:15,931 --> 00:40:17,571
No food, no happiness.

984
00:40:17,572 --> 00:40:20,418
No food, no happiness! Me too!

985
00:40:20,795 --> 00:40:21,820
Here.

986
00:40:22,228 --> 00:40:23,054
Open!

987
00:40:26,475 --> 00:40:28,335
(Goal)

988
00:40:28,362 --> 00:40:29,755
- Did you see that?
- What happened?

989
00:40:29,756 --> 00:40:31,162
- I threw it in her mouth!
- Try it!

990
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:34,046
(Trying to put it right in her mouth.)

991
00:40:34,673 --> 00:40:35,733
Say, ah!

992
00:40:37,626 --> 00:40:39,686
(Nom)

993
00:40:40,246 --> 00:40:42,466
(Never mind the look on her face!)

994
00:40:42,841 --> 00:40:44,042
- Well done!
- Did you see that?

995
00:40:44,043 --> 00:40:45,243
Yeah, I did.

996
00:40:45,321 --> 00:40:47,321
Calm down. Stop.

997
00:40:49,005 --> 00:40:50,994
She's heading under the tree.

998
00:40:51,307 --> 00:40:53,747
- I think she's itchy.
- Itchy!

999
00:40:53,748 --> 00:40:55,320
She's rubbing her back on it.

1000
00:40:55,321 --> 00:40:57,955
- How cute!
- She's happy.

1001
00:40:58,628 --> 00:41:00,263
I bet that felt great.

1002
00:41:00,264 --> 00:41:02,648
(How to be happy:
Fill your belly then scratch your back.)

1003
00:41:02,894 --> 00:41:05,358
Imagine how much it has to eat...

1004
00:41:05,359 --> 00:41:07,632
- to get full at that size.
- It'll have to eat so much.

1005
00:41:08,605 --> 00:41:11,135
Hey, girl. Here you go.

1006
00:41:11,252 --> 00:41:12,537
Was this one a girl?

1007
00:41:13,485 --> 00:41:14,939
This is a girls' trip!

1008
00:41:14,940 --> 00:41:16,774
I think they're all female.

1009
00:41:16,867 --> 00:41:18,376
She's sticking to her sister.

1010
00:41:18,614 --> 00:41:21,212
The baby doesn't eat that much.

1011
00:41:21,274 --> 00:41:22,580
So cute.

1012
00:41:23,281 --> 00:41:25,383
This isn't food.

1013
00:41:25,813 --> 00:41:27,418
She's touching her ear.

1014
00:41:27,759 --> 00:41:29,759
I'll give it to you.

1015
00:41:29,879 --> 00:41:31,256
(Eating slower and slower.)

1016
00:41:31,257 --> 00:41:32,590
Is she drooling?

1017
00:41:33,326 --> 00:41:34,559
(Staring)

1018
00:41:34,593 --> 00:41:37,829
Why are you playing with your food, Lucy?

1019
00:41:38,296 --> 00:41:41,532
You're gonna get in trouble
for playing with your food!

1020
00:41:41,744 --> 00:41:42,997
"I won't."

1021
00:41:42,998 --> 00:41:44,371
(I'll take that first, Mom.)

1022
00:41:44,736 --> 00:41:45,737
She's so cute.

1023
00:41:45,738 --> 00:41:47,004
(Little troublemaker)

1024
00:41:47,157 --> 00:41:48,239
Look at that.

1025
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:50,651
(And now she's raiding the food sack.)

1026
00:41:50,652 --> 00:41:52,812
Lucy!

1027
00:41:52,813 --> 00:41:53,856
- Cute.
- She really is a baby!

1028
00:41:54,779 --> 00:41:55,746
It's such a baby.

1029
00:41:55,747 --> 00:41:58,482
I guess it's not hungry.
It just wants to dig around in this.

1030
00:41:58,649 --> 00:42:01,329
- For now, they're almost full.
- Almost full.

1031
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:05,532
(With their belly full,
it's time for a walk.)

1032
00:42:05,557 --> 00:42:07,725
Now it's time to exercise.

1033
00:42:07,726 --> 00:42:08,826
Since they've eaten.

1034
00:42:09,059 --> 00:42:11,728
They're better than me.
They go for a walk right after eating.

1035
00:42:12,153 --> 00:42:13,779
- Go together.
- Okay.

1036
00:42:14,032 --> 00:42:15,866
- It's fascinating.
- Her little backside is so cute.

1037
00:42:15,867 --> 00:42:16,834
Exactly.

1038
00:42:17,168 --> 00:42:18,068
She's climbing a mountain.

1039
00:42:18,069 --> 00:42:19,478
Now, they enjoy free time.

1040
00:42:19,550 --> 00:42:21,070
- Out in nature.
- I feel really free.

1041
00:42:21,472 --> 00:42:23,707
To think I'm actually
taking a walk with an elephant...

1042
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:24,809
(A forest path walked with elephants)

1043
00:42:24,810 --> 00:42:25,742
Amazing.

1044
00:42:27,111 --> 00:42:28,612
It's so cool and refreshing here.

1045
00:42:28,613 --> 00:42:29,579
Absolutely.

1046
00:42:30,181 --> 00:42:31,615
You look just like Moana.

1047
00:42:31,851 --> 00:42:32,849
I know.

1048
00:42:33,618 --> 00:42:35,252
(The OST immediately starts playing.)

1049
00:42:35,253 --> 00:42:36,753
It looks like you're the one
ruling this place.

1050
00:42:37,155 --> 00:42:40,357
(The Scorpion Captain
leading the elephants)

1051
00:42:40,992 --> 00:42:43,603
(The elephants suddenly stop.)

1052
00:42:43,628 --> 00:42:46,162
Look at that. They're gathering
dirt with their trunk and feet.

1053
00:42:46,163 --> 00:42:47,263
What are they doing?

1054
00:42:47,765 --> 00:42:49,599
- To spray it on their back.
- Look.

1055
00:42:51,469 --> 00:42:53,570
(Whoosh)

1056
00:42:53,705 --> 00:42:54,972
They are doing it to keep...

1057
00:42:54,973 --> 00:42:57,008
(The two elephants take turns
spraying dirt over themselves.)

1058
00:42:57,009 --> 00:42:58,495
mosquitoes and flies from them.

1059
00:42:58,496 --> 00:42:59,761
That's happy life.

1060
00:43:00,272 --> 00:43:02,319
Indeed, that's happy life.

1061
00:43:02,996 --> 00:43:04,496
It'll let them have a long life.

1062
00:43:05,033 --> 00:43:07,585
So doing this helps them live longer.

1063
00:43:10,189 --> 00:43:11,956
They gather the dirt like this, and...

1064
00:43:12,690 --> 00:43:14,457
(Do you really have to do all that?)

1065
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:15,859
They gather the dirt...

1066
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:18,361
- They use both their feet and trunk.
- I know.

1067
00:43:18,362 --> 00:43:20,930
They gather like this.

1068
00:43:21,165 --> 00:43:21,998
(Let's go.)

1069
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:24,167
(She's doing it well.)

1070
00:43:24,302 --> 00:43:26,436
Grandma definitely has a lot of wisdom.

1071
00:43:26,972 --> 00:43:29,039
(The amount of dirt
she gathers is noticeably different.)

1072
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:31,075
She even knows how to use her feet.

1073
00:43:32,877 --> 00:43:34,477
- It's so cute.
- It's so cute.

1074
00:43:34,478 --> 00:43:35,848
(The baby elephant is
still clumsy with her trunk.)

1075
00:43:35,849 --> 00:43:36,713
It's so cute.

1076
00:43:37,759 --> 00:43:38,892
She's pooping.

1077
00:43:39,227 --> 00:43:41,452
It's green. It's matcha poop.

1078
00:43:42,220 --> 00:43:45,323
(The poop they'd been waiting
to see since feeding time.)

1079
00:43:45,973 --> 00:43:47,456
I can't believe
I'm seeing this in real life.

1080
00:43:47,457 --> 00:43:48,499
Now, waterfall.

1081
00:43:50,428 --> 00:43:51,328
(Whoosh)

1082
00:43:51,329 --> 00:43:53,663
- It's peeing too.
- At the same time!

1083
00:43:53,664 --> 00:43:57,605
(A master of the bowel movement routine)

1084
00:43:59,604 --> 00:44:01,271
Am I really allowed to watch this?

1085
00:44:02,840 --> 00:44:04,450
(It's okay to watch, right?)

1086
00:44:04,475 --> 00:44:06,609
The angle right now is insane.

1087
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:10,313
She's had such a sheltered upbringing.
Is it okay for her to see?

1088
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:11,347
(The world really has
come a long way, hasn't it?)

1089
00:44:11,348 --> 00:44:14,350
You ate a lot of greens.
That must feel so refreshing.

1090
00:44:14,786 --> 00:44:16,621
(Her complexion looks even better now.)

1091
00:44:16,622 --> 00:44:17,912
- We shall go.
- Let's go now.

1092
00:44:18,390 --> 00:44:20,391
- It's interesting.
- I saw an elephant poop.

1093
00:44:20,392 --> 00:44:21,959
- Amazing.
- I saw that in person.

1094
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:23,994
(A sight you'd never
get to see anywhere else)

1095
00:44:24,262 --> 00:44:26,063
I'm honestly jealous.

1096
00:44:26,064 --> 00:44:27,464
She poops immediately after eating.

1097
00:44:27,465 --> 00:44:28,632
It's like a straight pipe.

1098
00:44:28,766 --> 00:44:31,534
And there were bubbles,
so it kind of looked like matcha foam.

1099
00:44:31,535 --> 00:44:33,536
(The lingering impression
doesn't fade easily.)

1100
00:44:34,575 --> 00:44:36,306
(The elephants get excited
when they reach the muddy water.)

1101
00:44:36,307 --> 00:44:38,909
It's so cute how they have
dirt piled all over their backs.

1102
00:44:40,245 --> 00:44:43,514
(They splash muddy water
all over their bodies.)

1103
00:44:43,581 --> 00:44:45,115
Apparently, it protects their skin,

1104
00:44:45,116 --> 00:44:46,314
but they also do it just for fun.

1105
00:44:47,385 --> 00:44:48,785
- Just for fun?
- Exactly.

1106
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:50,220
It looks fun.

1107
00:44:50,322 --> 00:44:53,623
That's why their skin stays moist
instead of getting dry.

1108
00:44:53,791 --> 00:44:54,958
Are they hot?

1109
00:44:54,959 --> 00:44:56,559
(Splash)

1110
00:44:56,695 --> 00:44:58,462
It's a water slap.

1111
00:44:58,463 --> 00:45:00,130
- It's a water slap.
- They're so excited.

1112
00:45:00,131 --> 00:45:03,200
(An elephant giving a water slap)

1113
00:45:03,835 --> 00:45:05,035
Well done.

1114
00:45:05,036 --> 00:45:06,303
(Fan service)

1115
00:45:06,704 --> 00:45:09,239
- As expected, Grandma has the skills.
- Exactly.

1116
00:45:09,240 --> 00:45:10,540
Come here, Harimu.

1117
00:45:10,742 --> 00:45:11,775
What's this?

1118
00:45:12,410 --> 00:45:14,111
I got poop on my face.

1119
00:45:14,112 --> 00:45:15,012
(Playing in the mud with the elephants)

1120
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:17,248
And this one is
just by herself over here...

1121
00:45:17,273 --> 00:45:18,407
She's having such a good time
all by herself.

1122
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:20,683
She looks incredibly moisturized.

1123
00:45:20,684 --> 00:45:23,087
She must have put on
a whole bottle of ampoule.

1124
00:45:23,088 --> 00:45:25,722
- It's so moisturized.
- It's a mud facial

1125
00:45:25,723 --> 00:45:26,990
So cute.

1126
00:45:26,991 --> 00:45:29,125
That looks like so much fun.

1127
00:45:30,028 --> 00:45:31,195
Her feet are so cute.

1128
00:45:31,196 --> 00:45:32,529
Absolutely.

1129
00:45:32,530 --> 00:45:34,164
Even the way she walks is adorable.

1130
00:45:35,033 --> 00:45:37,501
It's amazing. I never thought
I'd get to see them this close.

1131
00:45:37,502 --> 00:45:40,070
(A unique experience in Chiang Mai)

1132
00:45:40,071 --> 00:45:41,705
I really feel like we're connecting.

1133
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:43,306
Exactly.

1134
00:45:43,474 --> 00:45:45,075
I like elephants even more now.

1135
00:45:46,222 --> 00:45:49,226
After eating, they have energy from food
to work.

1136
00:45:50,181 --> 00:45:51,081
I see.

1137
00:45:51,149 --> 00:45:52,750
(Then the elephant suddenly lies down.)

1138
00:45:52,751 --> 00:45:55,452
- Look, she suddenly lies down.
- Is she doing a mud mask?

1139
00:45:56,087 --> 00:45:58,021
- Did she fall?
- She fell down.

1140
00:45:58,022 --> 00:45:58,989
She's just lying down.

1141
00:45:59,223 --> 00:46:00,190
Because she's feeling good.

1142
00:46:00,391 --> 00:46:03,494
- She's hilarious.
- She's just lying down.

1143
00:46:03,865 --> 00:46:05,529
- This baby...
- It's a floor performance.

1144
00:46:05,830 --> 00:46:07,163
Floor performance?

1145
00:46:07,164 --> 00:46:11,001
(The encouragement makes the dance
even more energetic.)

1146
00:46:11,002 --> 00:46:13,170
She must be really enjoying herself.

1147
00:46:13,171 --> 00:46:15,874
You'll need a good wash later.

1148
00:46:16,007 --> 00:46:19,476
(An elephant party for everyone.)

1149
00:46:19,477 --> 00:46:22,861
(The elephant club
loved by all generations)

1150
00:46:25,016 --> 00:46:26,817
(Sliding)

1151
00:46:27,152 --> 00:46:29,219
- It's cute.
- It's really cute.

1152
00:46:29,353 --> 00:46:30,953
I can't believe I'm seeing this.

1153
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:33,166
(The baby elephant gently
lies down beside her.)

1154
00:46:33,895 --> 00:46:35,024
They're scratching each other.

1155
00:46:36,094 --> 00:46:39,930
They sit down while scratching each other.

1156
00:46:40,933 --> 00:46:42,265
This is crazy.

1157
00:46:42,266 --> 00:46:43,133
(Deeply moved)

1158
00:46:43,134 --> 00:46:44,935
She's doing it again.

1159
00:46:44,936 --> 00:46:47,404
- It's so cute.
- She must really love it.

1160
00:46:47,405 --> 00:46:48,806
I think so.

1161
00:46:51,142 --> 00:46:52,214
(Successfully slides down)

1162
00:46:52,215 --> 00:46:54,134
Yes, have fun together!

1163
00:46:54,245 --> 00:46:55,279
It really is a party.

1164
00:46:55,613 --> 00:46:56,546
What a scene.

1165
00:46:56,547 --> 00:46:59,868
(Everyone is soon lost
in their own little world.)

1166
00:46:59,881 --> 00:47:02,487
- It's really cute.
- It's so cute.

1167
00:47:03,254 --> 00:47:04,321
It's so cute.

1168
00:47:04,322 --> 00:47:05,255
Unbelievable.

1169
00:47:05,723 --> 00:47:07,157
Is this kind of a party trick?

1170
00:47:07,358 --> 00:47:09,759
Girls, look over here.

1171
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:12,128
All of them are lying down.

1172
00:47:12,129 --> 00:47:14,597
(Human girls and elephant girls)

1173
00:47:15,032 --> 00:47:17,734
They really love playing around
in areas like this.

1174
00:47:19,065 --> 00:47:21,491
- I can't believe it.
- It's unbelievable, right?

1175
00:47:22,031 --> 00:47:24,797
I heard that an elephant has
its own character.

1176
00:47:24,798 --> 00:47:26,378
One elephant, one personality.

1177
00:47:27,545 --> 00:47:29,072
How different they are?

1178
00:47:29,113 --> 00:47:31,381
First of all, Grandma elephant is...

1179
00:47:31,382 --> 00:47:32,916
The grandma elephant?

1180
00:47:32,917 --> 00:47:35,085
She's a little bit shy sometimes.

1181
00:47:35,086 --> 00:47:36,486
(Grandma elephant is a little shy.)

1182
00:47:36,687 --> 00:47:38,488
Lucy loves to eat.

1183
00:47:39,357 --> 00:47:40,457
(The baby elephant loves bananas.)

1184
00:47:40,458 --> 00:47:42,559
She's still a baby, so she's growing.

1185
00:47:43,327 --> 00:47:44,628
Chai Lai loves...

1186
00:47:45,464 --> 00:47:48,131
playing with the water.

1187
00:47:48,156 --> 00:47:50,635
(Older sister loves playing with water.)

1188
00:47:50,728 --> 00:47:52,092
- It's cute.
- See? One more time.

1189
00:47:52,136 --> 00:47:54,738
(They've found another mud paradise.)

1190
00:47:54,839 --> 00:47:57,874
They really look so happy.

1191
00:47:57,875 --> 00:48:00,076
- So cute.
- This place is kind of like a slide.

1192
00:48:00,101 --> 00:48:03,013
(The elephants are
free to play in the mud.)

1193
00:48:03,181 --> 00:48:04,848
They're so cute. What do I do?

1194
00:48:05,249 --> 00:48:06,082
So cute.

1195
00:48:06,317 --> 00:48:08,451
They're going crazy,
even getting down on their knees.

1196
00:48:09,086 --> 00:48:10,420
They're just so happy.

1197
00:48:10,821 --> 00:48:11,888
They're drinking water.

1198
00:48:12,156 --> 00:48:13,723
They're really just like people.

1199
00:48:14,292 --> 00:48:16,426
They eat and play, then drink some water.

1200
00:48:16,595 --> 00:48:18,995
They look like the happiest animals
I've ever seen.

1201
00:48:18,996 --> 00:48:20,096
Absolutely.

1202
00:48:20,097 --> 00:48:21,197
(The baby keeps playing with her trunk.)

1203
00:48:21,198 --> 00:48:22,298
I'm kind of jealous too.

1204
00:48:23,834 --> 00:48:25,268
She's pooping again.

1205
00:48:25,570 --> 00:48:27,304
(Plop)

1206
00:48:27,305 --> 00:48:28,739
Eat, poop, and play.

1207
00:48:28,939 --> 00:48:31,274
Why are we so fascinated
by poop like a little kid?

1208
00:48:32,376 --> 00:48:33,242
Let's go now.

1209
00:48:33,844 --> 00:48:34,677
Time to wash up.

1210
00:48:36,224 --> 00:48:37,513
There's another pill bug here.

1211
00:48:38,316 --> 00:48:39,616
You spotted that right away?

1212
00:48:39,617 --> 00:48:40,550
Yes, right here.

1213
00:48:40,595 --> 00:48:41,461
(A giant pill bug)

1214
00:48:41,485 --> 00:48:42,485
- A pill bug.
- What happened?

1215
00:48:42,720 --> 00:48:44,054
There's a pill bug here.

1216
00:48:44,852 --> 00:48:45,722
Another roly-poly.

1217
00:48:45,723 --> 00:48:47,291
(Every kid's instinct
when they see a pill bug)

1218
00:48:47,292 --> 00:48:48,225
Great job.

1219
00:48:48,270 --> 00:48:50,927
(You have a real talent for that.)

1220
00:48:51,429 --> 00:48:53,830
(Walking alongside the elephants)

1221
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:55,932
- Are you blocking the road?
- Blocking...

1222
00:48:55,933 --> 00:48:57,000
- Are you blocking the road?
- Are you?

1223
00:48:57,668 --> 00:48:59,602
Suddenly, she's eating grass?

1224
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:01,437
(They suddenly charge
into the forest to eat grass.)

1225
00:49:01,438 --> 00:49:02,673
They suddenly go that way.

1226
00:49:02,674 --> 00:49:05,341
They're eating these bamboo plants.

1227
00:49:05,455 --> 00:49:06,568
Bamboo.

1228
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:08,711
The elephants are blazing a trail.

1229
00:49:10,281 --> 00:49:11,247
That's exactly my inspiration.

1230
00:49:12,283 --> 00:49:13,149
"Inspiration."

1231
00:49:13,517 --> 00:49:15,919
- You're my inspiration, elephants.
- Elephant in Chiang Mai.

1232
00:49:16,857 --> 00:49:19,189
Ellie.

1233
00:49:19,190 --> 00:49:21,725
- The walk is over.
- We came back to where we had our meal.

1234
00:49:21,726 --> 00:49:23,360
We took a big loop around.

1235
00:49:23,728 --> 00:49:24,594
Absolutely.

1236
00:49:24,662 --> 00:49:26,195
We came back to where we had our meal.

1237
00:49:26,364 --> 00:49:29,099
When else would I ever get
to go for a walk with elephants?

1238
00:49:29,100 --> 00:49:30,367
That's right.

1239
00:49:30,368 --> 00:49:33,437
This is the first time I've ever done this
in my 18 years of traveling.

1240
00:49:34,739 --> 00:49:36,773
They're going to take a bath.

1241
00:49:37,174 --> 00:49:38,608
Let's go together.

1242
00:49:39,210 --> 00:49:43,946
(Finally, the elephant bathing session)

1243
00:49:44,115 --> 00:49:47,717
(She waddles toward the water
all by herself.)

1244
00:49:50,634 --> 00:49:52,639
It's shower time...

1245
00:49:52,640 --> 00:49:53,940
with me!

1246
00:49:54,492 --> 00:49:57,961
(Entering the river
together with the elephants)

1247
00:49:57,962 --> 00:50:00,001
Oh, my goodness, so muddy!

1248
00:50:00,798 --> 00:50:03,409
(They can feel the soft,
wet mud beneath their feet.)

1249
00:50:03,434 --> 00:50:05,468
I'm so excited. Be careful.

1250
00:50:06,303 --> 00:50:10,306
(Here comes the Grandma.)

1251
00:50:10,721 --> 00:50:12,374
Okay, let's go.

1252
00:50:12,443 --> 00:50:15,321
(The baby is already sitting
in the water.)

1253
00:50:15,346 --> 00:50:17,213
Did she sit down?

1254
00:50:18,449 --> 00:50:19,582
Look, she's lying down.

1255
00:50:20,918 --> 00:50:22,118
Look, she's lying down.

1256
00:50:22,186 --> 00:50:24,154
(Diving)

1257
00:50:24,155 --> 00:50:25,622
It's adorable.

1258
00:50:27,425 --> 00:50:31,662
(Water play begins.)

1259
00:50:32,196 --> 00:50:33,663
(Looking around)

1260
00:50:33,664 --> 00:50:34,464
(Spit)

1261
00:50:35,700 --> 00:50:36,833
(Spit)

1262
00:50:37,268 --> 00:50:39,669
(The funniest face)

1263
00:50:40,237 --> 00:50:42,405
(An absolute delight
for everyone watching)

1264
00:50:44,075 --> 00:50:46,476
(Cool, refreshing water playtime)

1265
00:50:46,477 --> 00:50:47,644
So cute.

1266
00:50:50,531 --> 00:50:51,471
Let's go.

1267
00:50:51,472 --> 00:50:52,831
(Splash)

1268
00:50:54,619 --> 00:50:57,087
Let's have a water fight together.

1269
00:51:00,858 --> 00:51:02,025
This is ridiculous.

1270
00:51:02,026 --> 00:51:05,528
(She sprays a refreshing stream of water.)

1271
00:51:06,263 --> 00:51:08,931
(Her face is all scrunched up.)

1272
00:51:09,543 --> 00:51:11,290
- How cute.
- Argh!

1273
00:51:13,070 --> 00:51:17,273
(There are so many ways
to scare yourself.)

1274
00:51:17,274 --> 00:51:18,741
Hey.

1275
00:51:20,077 --> 00:51:21,511
(The water spray has very little impact.)

1276
00:51:21,512 --> 00:51:22,612
(Slip)

1277
00:51:25,783 --> 00:51:27,951
(Whatever)

1278
00:51:28,886 --> 00:51:29,719
(What were you doing?)

1279
00:51:30,054 --> 00:51:32,088
I have no idea.

1280
00:51:32,723 --> 00:51:33,456
(Swoosh)

1281
00:51:33,457 --> 00:51:35,958
(Chiang Mai Waterbomb)

1282
00:51:35,959 --> 00:51:36,859
Hold on.

1283
00:51:37,962 --> 00:51:40,564
Who's showering whom?

1284
00:51:41,074 --> 00:51:43,466
(Obviously, an elephant shower.)

1285
00:51:44,568 --> 00:51:47,136
(The baby elephant seems to want
to wash them more.)

1286
00:51:47,137 --> 00:51:50,640
(Harimu is having the time of her life.)

1287
00:51:50,964 --> 00:51:53,542
(Laughing)

1288
00:51:54,056 --> 00:51:56,741
(She sits down in front of the elephant,
slightly nervous.)

1289
00:51:57,781 --> 00:51:59,934
(The elephants hug her.)

1290
00:51:59,935 --> 00:52:00,951
Thank you.

1291
00:52:03,901 --> 00:52:05,222
Thank you!

1292
00:52:05,635 --> 00:52:07,355
- A kiss!
- A kiss!

1293
00:52:07,455 --> 00:52:10,728
- A kiss!
- A kiss!

1294
00:52:10,768 --> 00:52:12,129
- A kiss!
- A kiss!

1295
00:52:13,008 --> 00:52:15,288
(A light peck)

1296
00:52:15,854 --> 00:52:17,393
(On the other cheek)

1297
00:52:17,401 --> 00:52:17,928
(Smack!)

1298
00:52:19,068 --> 00:52:20,381
(Smack!)

1299
00:52:20,881 --> 00:52:22,806
I could hear the smacking sound.

1300
00:52:22,974 --> 00:52:24,974
She made a smacking sound like an effect.

1301
00:52:26,039 --> 00:52:28,386
One more.

1302
00:52:28,659 --> 00:52:29,474
One more!

1303
00:52:29,474 --> 00:52:31,090
(This touch elephant prepares
another kiss.)

1304
00:52:31,352 --> 00:52:32,618
(Spraying water)

1305
00:52:32,886 --> 00:52:36,770
(Laughter bursting out)

1306
00:52:37,230 --> 00:52:39,843
(Pretending to give her a kiss,
then spraying her with water)

1307
00:52:40,383 --> 00:52:43,093
Hey! You're funny.

1308
00:52:43,417 --> 00:52:45,062
- That's so hilarious.
- You're funny.

1309
00:52:45,727 --> 00:52:46,829
(Yes, it was.)

1310
00:52:46,830 --> 00:52:48,165
That was hilarious.

1311
00:52:48,523 --> 00:52:50,223
(Curling her trunk)

1312
00:52:57,408 --> 00:52:58,377
(Spraying)

1313
00:52:59,330 --> 00:53:01,163
(Spraying water)

1314
00:53:01,839 --> 00:53:03,189
(They're like a comedy duo.)

1315
00:53:03,709 --> 00:53:05,449
You don't like me, do you?

1316
00:53:06,136 --> 00:53:06,936
Is that why?

1317
00:53:08,575 --> 00:53:09,456
(Sneaky)

1318
00:53:09,522 --> 00:53:10,387
(Spraying)

1319
00:53:11,276 --> 00:53:13,190
What's with her?

1320
00:53:13,980 --> 00:53:15,492
What's with this lady?

1321
00:53:15,534 --> 00:53:17,962
Hey, we were good earlier.

1322
00:53:19,563 --> 00:53:20,831
I want to hug her too.

1323
00:53:21,519 --> 00:53:22,587
Hi!

1324
00:53:22,814 --> 00:53:24,611
(The elephants give her a warm hug.)

1325
00:53:25,458 --> 00:53:27,584
(Kissing her on both cheeks at once)

1326
00:53:27,585 --> 00:53:28,545
(Sucking)

1327
00:53:29,191 --> 00:53:31,258
(That sounded like a vacuum.)

1328
00:53:31,318 --> 00:53:32,176
Come on.

1329
00:53:32,177 --> 00:53:32,805
(A peck)

1330
00:53:33,405 --> 00:53:34,678
(I like you.)

1331
00:53:35,198 --> 00:53:36,776
(Gabee, what about me?)

1332
00:53:37,096 --> 00:53:39,003
(Spraying immediately)

1333
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:40,851
That's so funny.

1334
00:53:42,453 --> 00:53:45,316
(Giving her a hug
after spraying her with water)

1335
00:53:45,409 --> 00:53:48,054
- I got it. Please stop.
- Give her a hug.

1336
00:53:49,134 --> 00:53:50,333
(They hug Won Ji first.)

1337
00:53:50,334 --> 00:53:52,467
(Awkward)

1338
00:53:52,967 --> 00:53:54,947
(As she feels awkward,
they give her a peck.)

1339
00:53:55,421 --> 00:53:56,694
(That was so much water!)

1340
00:53:56,754 --> 00:53:58,102
That cleans your ears.

1341
00:53:58,103 --> 00:53:59,901
(The perk of an elephant kiss is
getting your ears cleaned.)

1342
00:54:01,947 --> 00:54:03,540
As much as you love her!

1343
00:54:04,347 --> 00:54:05,676
That scared me.

1344
00:54:05,677 --> 00:54:07,214
(Did you think it was over?)

1345
00:54:08,167 --> 00:54:09,614
(Grabbing her by the neck)

1346
00:54:09,701 --> 00:54:11,301
(A peck)

1347
00:54:11,354 --> 00:54:13,687
(An intense neck-grab kiss)

1348
00:54:14,541 --> 00:54:16,528
It's cold!

1349
00:54:16,668 --> 00:54:17,921
(Staring)

1350
00:54:17,922 --> 00:54:19,023
You're going to keep doing that?

1351
00:54:20,654 --> 00:54:22,126
You'll keep doing that?

1352
00:54:22,133 --> 00:54:23,853
(We're 30cm away.)

1353
00:54:23,854 --> 00:54:25,526
(Another water bomb)

1354
00:54:26,092 --> 00:54:27,598
Hey!

1355
00:54:29,252 --> 00:54:30,799
(Responding by spraying water)

1356
00:54:31,046 --> 00:54:32,369
That's so funny.

1357
00:54:35,019 --> 00:54:37,019
There you go! Thanks.

1358
00:54:37,352 --> 00:54:38,475
Thank you so much.

1359
00:54:38,476 --> 00:54:39,977
One more time!

1360
00:54:40,408 --> 00:54:41,979
That's great.

1361
00:54:41,980 --> 00:54:44,289
It sounded intense. Are you all right?

1362
00:54:44,343 --> 00:54:45,315
Sian, do you want to go?

1363
00:54:45,316 --> 00:54:47,317
I'm so scared.

1364
00:54:47,397 --> 00:54:49,553
You can do it. It's not that bad.

1365
00:54:51,030 --> 00:54:52,370
(Spraying water as soon as she sits down)

1366
00:54:52,936 --> 00:54:55,541
- This is so funny.
- She loves her so much.

1367
00:54:55,542 --> 00:54:56,593
It's cracking me up.

1368
00:54:56,643 --> 00:54:59,730
- Sian, you love elephants.
- You love elephants.

1369
00:55:00,110 --> 00:55:02,403
(As much as she loves them,
she can't stop frowning.)

1370
00:55:03,670 --> 00:55:06,050
(Nothing really happened,
and she's already terrified.)

1371
00:55:06,763 --> 00:55:08,038
I hate it so much!

1372
00:55:09,770 --> 00:55:13,043
I've become a huge fan of elephants.

1373
00:55:13,583 --> 00:55:16,983
I've really come to love elephants.

1374
00:55:17,070 --> 00:55:20,517
I just love elephants. I have to see them.

1375
00:55:24,417 --> 00:55:25,766
You're not a fan anymore?

1376
00:55:26,356 --> 00:55:27,558
Do you love elephants?

1377
00:55:28,192 --> 00:55:30,023
- I don't.
- She's not a fan anymore.

1378
00:55:30,024 --> 00:55:31,195
Are you falling out of love?

1379
00:55:31,465 --> 00:55:33,084
- A kiss!
- A kiss!

1380
00:55:33,085 --> 00:55:34,518
(Still, she's trying.)

1381
00:55:35,165 --> 00:55:37,657
(Frowning)

1382
00:55:38,071 --> 00:55:40,605
(Her heart says yes, but body says no.)

1383
00:55:42,112 --> 00:55:43,552
(Sulky)

1384
00:55:43,784 --> 00:55:45,784
Okay. Give me a peck.

1385
00:55:45,943 --> 00:55:46,812
(Sulky splashing)

1386
00:55:47,852 --> 00:55:49,272
(Spraying water
instead of giving her a peck)

1387
00:55:49,763 --> 00:55:51,923
Let her give you a kiss.

1388
00:55:52,310 --> 00:55:55,036
(She puckers up,
but keeps pushing them away.)

1389
00:55:55,616 --> 00:55:57,810
That's so funny.

1390
00:55:57,890 --> 00:56:00,224
I'm sorry. I really can't do this.

1391
00:56:00,383 --> 00:56:01,743
I just can't.

1392
00:56:01,744 --> 00:56:03,050
(Apologizing for falling out of love
with elephants)

1393
00:56:03,736 --> 00:56:06,003
(Spraying the elephants with water
like a mole)

1394
00:56:13,862 --> 00:56:15,472
Let's go!

1395
00:56:18,976 --> 00:56:22,312
Doesn't this feel nice?

1396
00:56:26,550 --> 00:56:28,252
Thank you.

1397
00:56:28,253 --> 00:56:29,584
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1398
00:56:29,585 --> 00:56:31,244
(They finish the refreshing shower.)

1399
00:56:34,270 --> 00:56:36,460
- I didn't expect this.
- Me neither.

1400
00:56:38,077 --> 00:56:40,842
- We might have to go to a souvenir shop.
- I know.

1401
00:56:40,843 --> 00:56:42,650
- That was so much fun.
- It was.

1402
00:56:42,684 --> 00:56:44,368
I've never done anything like this before.

1403
00:56:44,369 --> 00:56:45,244
Me neither.

1404
00:56:45,344 --> 00:56:46,970
Harimu was like Moana.

1405
00:56:47,423 --> 00:56:48,438
She really enjoyed it.

1406
00:56:48,478 --> 00:56:49,973
You looked like
you'd lived here for three years.

1407
00:56:50,037 --> 00:56:51,771
It just felt so familiar.

1408
00:56:51,772 --> 00:56:54,578
You look like you're a manager here.

1409
00:56:55,699 --> 00:56:56,980
Look at the way she's standing.

1410
00:56:57,139 --> 00:56:59,139
She's definitely from here.

1411
00:56:59,212 --> 00:57:02,619
Anyway, everyone. Welcome!

1412
00:57:02,620 --> 00:57:04,969
Our elephants are so friendly.

1413
00:57:04,970 --> 00:57:06,856
Thank you. We really had a good time.

1414
00:57:06,857 --> 00:57:08,458
- Please come again.
- Thank you.

1415
00:57:08,459 --> 00:57:10,994
It's nice to meet some Koreans.

1416
00:57:11,233 --> 00:57:13,030
I didn't know
my clothes would get like this.

1417
00:57:13,119 --> 00:57:15,532
- We had no idea.
- Seriously.

1418
00:57:15,579 --> 00:57:16,967
- Let's shower now.
- Sounds good.

1419
00:57:16,993 --> 00:57:18,535
It's our turn to take a shower.

1420
00:57:19,542 --> 00:57:22,080
- Not the elephants.
- I'm not sure who showered who.

1421
00:57:22,081 --> 00:57:23,340
Time for the humans to shower.

1422
00:57:23,341 --> 00:57:25,275
- Let's go now.
- Okay!

1423
00:57:25,276 --> 00:57:26,988
(It's time for them to take a shower.)

1424
00:57:27,854 --> 00:57:31,061
(Returning to their lodge
completely soaked)

1425
00:57:31,341 --> 00:57:33,341
We look so bad.

1426
00:57:36,486 --> 00:57:37,700
- Let's take a shower.
- Let's shower.

1427
00:57:37,754 --> 00:57:40,157
Please put your wet clothes here.

1428
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:43,147
(They'll freshen up
before their next activity.)

1429
00:57:43,427 --> 00:57:46,296
I'm just going to wear my pajamas.

1430
00:57:46,297 --> 00:57:49,233
(Out of clean clothes
after just three days)

1431
00:57:49,591 --> 00:57:51,768
That was so much fun.

1432
00:57:51,857 --> 00:57:53,270
All my stress just melted away.

1433
00:57:54,091 --> 00:57:59,043
(Unpacking their things
from their one suitcase)

1434
00:58:00,616 --> 00:58:02,196
(The members leave Won Ji alone.)

1435
00:58:02,197 --> 00:58:03,614
Is everyone leaving?

1436
00:58:04,223 --> 00:58:05,649
Yes. You can shower first.

1437
00:58:05,723 --> 00:58:06,783
We're locking you up.

1438
00:58:08,548 --> 00:58:10,621
- Locking you up!
- Locking you up!

1439
00:58:11,201 --> 00:58:12,588
It's not cold here.

1440
00:58:13,148 --> 00:58:16,408
(They showered one by one,
starting with the oldest.)

1441
00:58:16,541 --> 00:58:19,463
This is insanely refreshing!

1442
00:58:19,712 --> 00:58:22,065
- It's super refreshing.
- Totally.

1443
00:58:22,699 --> 00:58:24,801
We can hang our clothes there.

1444
00:58:26,570 --> 00:58:29,439
The water is so dirty.

1445
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:31,400
(Neatly hanging up...)

1446
00:58:32,220 --> 00:58:35,073
(the clothes they hand-washed
while showering)

1447
00:58:35,074 --> 00:58:36,094
(Wringing)

1448
00:58:38,800 --> 00:58:41,246
(Won Ji's UV arm sleeves)

1449
00:58:42,166 --> 00:58:47,200
(Hopefully, Chiang Mai's cool breeze
will dry our clothes.)

1450
00:58:48,586 --> 00:58:51,351
(A short break!)

1451
00:58:53,324 --> 00:58:55,631
(Turning on the camera)

1452
00:58:55,823 --> 00:58:57,434
Harimu, look here.

1453
00:59:00,370 --> 00:59:03,242
(Getting some downtime
for the first time in a while)

1454
00:59:03,515 --> 00:59:05,075
I forgot to bring pajamas.

1455
00:59:06,877 --> 00:59:08,679
I give up pajamas.

1456
00:59:09,202 --> 00:59:10,675
I'll give up everything.

1457
00:59:10,676 --> 00:59:11,823
(Won Ji gave up her pajamas.)

1458
00:59:12,255 --> 00:59:13,417
You didn't bring pajamas?

1459
00:59:13,418 --> 00:59:16,353
I just sleep in regular clothes.
They're pretty comfy.

1460
00:59:17,063 --> 00:59:18,388
You wear that pin a lot.

1461
00:59:20,589 --> 00:59:22,392
You have the same pin as me,
but you're using it a lot.

1462
00:59:23,042 --> 00:59:24,628
You said you didn't like it.

1463
00:59:24,629 --> 00:59:26,096
You sound like you're holding a grudge.

1464
00:59:27,642 --> 00:59:28,999
She said she didn't like it.

1465
00:59:29,382 --> 00:59:32,135
The cherry one is a snap clip,
and this one is a claw clip.

1466
00:59:32,136 --> 00:59:33,804
Oh, that is definitely more comfortable.

1467
00:59:34,016 --> 00:59:35,403
(Now she'd rather be comfy than cute.)

1468
00:59:35,404 --> 00:59:36,707
It's so useful.

1469
00:59:37,157 --> 00:59:38,508
You look really good.

1470
00:59:39,244 --> 00:59:40,744
We won't be scared tonight.

1471
00:59:42,317 --> 00:59:43,413
Because we're sleeping together.

1472
00:59:44,791 --> 00:59:46,144
(It's their first time sleeping
in the same room.)

1473
00:59:46,184 --> 00:59:47,851
You can sleep in the middle.

1474
00:59:48,384 --> 00:59:52,289
Let me lie down for a bit.

1475
00:59:52,923 --> 00:59:54,358
I want some gummies.

1476
00:59:54,915 --> 00:59:55,784
Gummies?

1477
00:59:55,963 --> 00:59:56,994
I have some.

1478
00:59:57,129 --> 00:59:58,695
- You do? Really?
- There.

1479
00:59:58,803 --> 01:00:00,703
I have some candy in my mesh bag.

1480
01:00:00,704 --> 01:00:01,944
(Won Ji has it all but pajamas.)

1481
01:00:01,945 --> 01:00:03,533
- Over there.
- This?

1482
01:00:03,609 --> 01:00:06,103
I have some candy and snacks.

1483
01:00:07,563 --> 01:00:08,872
A snack party!

1484
01:00:10,123 --> 01:00:12,616
I put the snacks we got
at the massage place in here.

1485
01:00:12,617 --> 01:00:13,977
We packed them all.

1486
01:00:13,978 --> 01:00:15,245
- Good job.
- They were good.

1487
01:00:15,246 --> 01:00:16,246
They're all yummy.

1488
01:00:16,895 --> 01:00:18,508
(Everyone gather for a sugar fix.)

1489
01:00:18,509 --> 01:00:19,349
It looks good.

1490
01:00:19,350 --> 01:00:21,904
(Feeding)

1491
01:00:22,683 --> 01:00:25,188
I want to see our pictures
with the elephants.

1492
01:00:25,256 --> 01:00:26,990
Me too. Let's send photos.

1493
01:00:28,002 --> 01:00:30,002
(Checking their pictures from earlier)

1494
01:00:30,236 --> 01:00:31,689
(Bursting into laughter)

1495
01:00:32,508 --> 01:00:35,949
(Check this out.)

1496
01:00:38,769 --> 01:00:41,304
"Aren't you scared of them?"

1497
01:00:41,305 --> 01:00:42,739
"Don't they scare you?"

1498
01:00:42,740 --> 01:00:43,740
Right.

1499
01:00:43,887 --> 01:00:45,208
She kept asking.

1500
01:00:45,674 --> 01:00:49,112
It was her first time touching them,
but she wasn't afraid at all.

1501
01:00:49,446 --> 01:00:52,527
Now I hate elephants.

1502
01:00:52,594 --> 01:00:54,484
She's officially done with them.

1503
01:00:54,485 --> 01:00:56,586
- I hate elephants.
- You're not a fan anymore.

1504
01:00:57,672 --> 01:00:58,659
(Laughing)

1505
01:01:03,894 --> 01:01:09,694
(Her scared face gets them every time.)

1506
01:01:13,200 --> 01:01:17,581
(Watching their videos over and over)

1507
01:01:18,834 --> 01:01:19,910
She's not a fan.

1508
01:01:19,911 --> 01:01:22,081
(Out of breath)

1509
01:01:22,674 --> 01:01:23,780
That was so funny.

1510
01:01:23,781 --> 01:01:25,781
I can't wait.

1511
01:01:25,782 --> 01:01:27,984
(They kept laughing for a while.)

1512
01:01:27,985 --> 01:01:29,659
- Really?
- Seriously.

1513
01:01:30,312 --> 01:01:32,165
(They laughed so hard
that they had no energy left.)

1514
01:01:32,319 --> 01:01:34,424
We should start changing.

1515
01:01:34,485 --> 01:01:35,926
I should change too.

1516
01:01:36,119 --> 01:01:37,260
We can't go out like this.

1517
01:01:37,305 --> 01:01:39,896
I'll wear more comfortable pants.

1518
01:01:40,632 --> 01:01:41,765
Do I have any clean clothes?

1519
01:01:42,525 --> 01:01:43,500
What are you going to do?

1520
01:01:43,800 --> 01:01:47,237
(Taking out the clothes she used before)

1521
01:01:47,746 --> 01:01:49,746
Hye Rim, that's a new look.

1522
01:01:49,786 --> 01:01:51,426
We've never seen you
in baggy clothes before.

1523
01:01:51,427 --> 01:01:52,926
Oh, that's my T-shirt.

1524
01:01:54,444 --> 01:01:55,968
(Harimu borrowed Won Ji's T-shirt.)

1525
01:01:55,969 --> 01:01:57,809
You look like a girl's hip hop dancer.

1526
01:01:58,515 --> 01:01:59,715
Shall we head out?

1527
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:01,217
Let's go.

1528
01:02:03,120 --> 01:02:06,089
(As the sun begins to set,
the air cools down.)

1529
01:02:07,791 --> 01:02:11,927
(To soak in this beautiful scenery,)

1530
01:02:15,265 --> 01:02:19,368
(they're off to a hilltop restaurant!)

1531
01:02:24,875 --> 01:02:26,375
Can we sit wherever?

1532
01:02:26,376 --> 01:02:28,311
Sure, I don't mind.

1533
01:02:28,478 --> 01:02:29,478
I'm so hungry!

1534
01:02:29,479 --> 01:02:31,680
- I'm hungry.
- Please feed us.

1535
01:02:31,681 --> 01:02:33,348
All that splashing around made us hungry.

1536
01:02:33,850 --> 01:02:36,685
How are we hungry nonstop?

1537
01:02:36,686 --> 01:02:37,853
Yeah, we're constantly hungry.

1538
01:02:38,221 --> 01:02:39,454
I want ramyeon.

1539
01:02:39,455 --> 01:02:41,590
I want meat. I'm a meat lover.

1540
01:02:42,025 --> 01:02:45,527
Meat sounds good too. I'll eat anything.

1541
01:02:45,729 --> 01:02:48,497
- They do this at Michelin restaurants.
- Really?

1542
01:02:48,498 --> 01:02:50,099
If they don't come, you do this.

1543
01:02:50,100 --> 01:02:51,434
(Flick)

1544
01:02:51,435 --> 01:02:52,968
And if that doesn't work, you do this.

1545
01:02:53,336 --> 01:02:54,770
Give us the menu, please.

1546
01:02:55,639 --> 01:02:56,606
(Can't help laughing)

1547
01:02:56,740 --> 01:02:57,743
You made that up, didn't you?

1548
01:02:58,141 --> 01:02:59,208
- Yes.
- A total liar.

1549
01:02:59,242 --> 01:02:59,975
What, really?

1550
01:02:59,976 --> 01:03:02,344
- But that actually seemed legit.
- Yeah.

1551
01:03:02,345 --> 01:03:04,913
(Right on cue, the menu arrives.)

1552
01:03:04,914 --> 01:03:06,415
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1553
01:03:06,416 --> 01:03:07,349
Thank you very much.

1554
01:03:07,350 --> 01:03:08,650
(Scanning menu)

1555
01:03:08,651 --> 01:03:10,786
- Thank you.
- One menu per person.

1556
01:03:11,354 --> 01:03:12,788
They have Korean barbecue.

1557
01:03:13,259 --> 01:03:15,024
- Where?
- Where?

1558
01:03:15,025 --> 01:03:16,059
On the back.

1559
01:03:16,626 --> 01:03:18,627
- Found it!
- They have seafood too.

1560
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:20,729
This is...

1561
01:03:20,864 --> 01:03:22,565
a Thai style barbecue called mookata.

1562
01:03:22,899 --> 01:03:25,101
- Thai style barbecue?
- Thai style Korean barbecue?

1563
01:03:25,102 --> 01:03:26,368
I'm kind of curious.

1564
01:03:26,369 --> 01:03:28,737
It seems like a combination
of Thai and Korean.

1565
01:03:28,738 --> 01:03:30,305
Right, like a fusion cuisine.

1566
01:03:30,541 --> 01:03:32,175
Should we try the barbecue?

1567
01:03:32,176 --> 01:03:33,476
- Yes.
- Yes.

1568
01:03:33,777 --> 01:03:36,011
We'll have one of these.

1569
01:03:36,313 --> 01:03:39,515
Thank you.

1570
01:03:39,849 --> 01:03:40,750
I'm excited.

1571
01:03:40,751 --> 01:03:41,684
It sounds yummy.

1572
01:03:41,685 --> 01:03:42,551
I'm hungry.

1573
01:03:42,552 --> 01:03:45,488
It's so nice just sitting here
and enjoying the view.

1574
01:03:45,489 --> 01:03:47,289
Don't you think it's giving Hawaii?

1575
01:03:48,558 --> 01:03:50,726
- This is so nice.
- It looks amazing.

1576
01:03:50,727 --> 01:03:51,527
(A lush forest stretches out
right behind them.)

1577
01:03:51,962 --> 01:03:53,796
Look at the sunset.

1578
01:03:54,498 --> 01:03:55,398
It's beautiful.

1579
01:03:55,399 --> 01:03:58,000
(The sky slowly fades into dusk.)

1580
01:03:58,001 --> 01:03:59,035
So beautiful.

1581
01:04:00,070 --> 01:04:01,003
I really enjoyed it here.

1582
01:04:01,404 --> 01:04:03,438
Yeah, Chiang Mai is heaps of fun.

1583
01:04:03,439 --> 01:04:04,539
(The sunset paints
the Elephant Hotel red.)

1584
01:04:04,808 --> 01:04:06,742
Look at our hotel.

1585
01:04:06,743 --> 01:04:08,878
We really hung up a lot of laundry.

1586
01:04:09,513 --> 01:04:10,681
That would look hilarious from the drone.

1587
01:04:10,682 --> 01:04:12,148
We're hanging our underwear out too.

1588
01:04:12,149 --> 01:04:13,015
You're right.

1589
01:04:13,483 --> 01:04:14,983
- Why not?
- Any problem?

1590
01:04:15,485 --> 01:04:16,552
What are you two wearing tomorrow?

1591
01:04:17,120 --> 01:04:19,555
As for us...

1592
01:04:19,556 --> 01:04:22,558
We haven't really decided yet.

1593
01:04:22,926 --> 01:04:24,326
That's because you have nothing left
to wear.

1594
01:04:24,327 --> 01:04:25,628
We really don't.

1595
01:04:26,396 --> 01:04:29,231
Trust me, I really want to wear
something awesome.

1596
01:04:29,599 --> 01:04:31,166
But this is all I've got.

1597
01:04:31,167 --> 01:04:32,034
(Given up)

1598
01:04:32,035 --> 01:04:34,369
- Your go-to outfit.
- If anyone had taken this off,

1599
01:04:34,437 --> 01:04:35,948
- I'd be completely naked now.
- I know.

1600
01:04:37,073 --> 01:04:37,939
That's right.

1601
01:04:38,575 --> 01:04:40,576
- That's right.
- These pants...

1602
01:04:40,577 --> 01:04:43,012
are the only thing I have.

1603
01:04:43,013 --> 01:04:44,346
It's killing me.

1604
01:04:45,249 --> 01:04:47,750
We basically know
what's inside our suitcase now.

1605
01:04:48,051 --> 01:04:49,719
It's so obvious!

1606
01:04:49,720 --> 01:04:51,487
There's not much left in there.

1607
01:04:51,655 --> 01:04:53,456
We all know what we brought now.

1608
01:04:53,457 --> 01:04:54,658
- We do.
- We know who brought what.

1609
01:04:54,659 --> 01:04:57,526
And we have no problem...

1610
01:04:57,527 --> 01:05:00,529
- using each other's items.
- We're really sharing everything.

1611
01:05:00,997 --> 01:05:04,032
You're wearing one of my T-shirts today.

1612
01:05:04,033 --> 01:05:06,668
Won Ji.

1613
01:05:06,937 --> 01:05:09,672
Even the arm sleeves are Won Ji's.

1614
01:05:09,673 --> 01:05:12,141
- Right.
- I realized something today.

1615
01:05:12,609 --> 01:05:14,209
When you go on backpacking trips,

1616
01:05:14,210 --> 01:05:15,844
the bags you take are huge.

1617
01:05:15,845 --> 01:05:17,813
We don't even need one of those.

1618
01:05:17,814 --> 01:05:19,582
We could travel
with just a regular backpack.

1619
01:05:19,583 --> 01:05:20,849
I totally agree.

1620
01:05:20,850 --> 01:05:22,518
I'm learning to let go of things.

1621
01:05:23,187 --> 01:05:24,420
You really threw out a lot.

1622
01:05:24,421 --> 01:05:26,423
You're not even using much makeup.

1623
01:05:26,424 --> 01:05:28,724
I used to carry all that
because I was anxious without them.

1624
01:05:29,060 --> 01:05:30,893
Turns out, you don't really need it all.

1625
01:05:30,894 --> 01:05:31,760
(Things that weren't necessary.)

1626
01:05:31,761 --> 01:05:33,963
I think I could really go on trips
with a backpack.

1627
01:05:34,864 --> 01:05:36,131
- For real.
- Let's do it.

1628
01:05:36,132 --> 01:05:37,566
Abra-ca-Empty, backpacking trip.

1629
01:05:39,869 --> 01:05:40,735
(Why aren't you saying anything?)

1630
01:05:40,736 --> 01:05:41,670
She doesn't like it.

1631
01:05:42,973 --> 01:05:46,142
(Let's see
if she can let go of even more.)

1632
01:05:47,777 --> 01:05:48,710
The food's here!

1633
01:05:49,079 --> 01:05:51,080
- It's here?
- It really is pork belly.

1634
01:05:51,081 --> 01:05:52,181
(Here comes mookata, Thai-style barbecue.)

1635
01:05:52,616 --> 01:05:53,916
Is he going to pour beaten eggs in here?

1636
01:05:54,317 --> 01:05:55,284
Beaten eggs.

1637
01:05:55,285 --> 01:05:56,885
- Or cheese.
- That actually makes sense.

1638
01:05:56,886 --> 01:05:57,986
(A grill with a recessed rim.)

1639
01:06:00,557 --> 01:06:01,757
There's fruit.

1640
01:06:01,758 --> 01:06:02,624
What's that for?

1641
01:06:04,227 --> 01:06:05,761
Thankfully, there's so much food.

1642
01:06:06,463 --> 01:06:07,663
This looks like pork shoulder.

1643
01:06:07,664 --> 01:06:08,964
(Familiar cuts of meat,
beautifully presented)

1644
01:06:08,965 --> 01:06:10,766
It looks like you won a prize!

1645
01:06:10,767 --> 01:06:11,867
Thank you so much.

1646
01:06:12,135 --> 01:06:12,968
I mean it.

1647
01:06:13,837 --> 01:06:15,171
- Wow, vegetables.
- What's this?

1648
01:06:15,172 --> 01:06:16,038
There's so much food.

1649
01:06:16,506 --> 01:06:18,640
There are broccoli and eggs.

1650
01:06:18,641 --> 01:06:19,541
What's this?

1651
01:06:21,378 --> 01:06:22,745
So it wasn't a grease trap!

1652
01:06:22,746 --> 01:06:23,679
Water.

1653
01:06:24,080 --> 01:06:24,980
Soup.

1654
01:06:24,981 --> 01:06:25,914
- Soup?
- Soup?

1655
01:06:25,915 --> 01:06:26,681
Yes.

1656
01:06:26,682 --> 01:06:28,517
(Wait, what?)

1657
01:06:29,185 --> 01:06:33,054
Once the water starts boiling,
add the vegetables around the grill.

1658
01:06:33,390 --> 01:06:34,490
I see.

1659
01:06:34,491 --> 01:06:36,359
Like a hotpot.

1660
01:06:36,893 --> 01:06:38,293
Guys, there're noodles too.

1661
01:06:38,764 --> 01:06:40,529
So that's what the rim is for.

1662
01:06:40,530 --> 01:06:42,164
(A Thai dish combining
grilled pork and hotpot.)

1663
01:06:43,233 --> 01:06:43,996
That's so interesting.

1664
01:06:44,267 --> 01:06:46,602
I'm really curious,
so I'm going to try the broth.

1665
01:06:46,603 --> 01:06:47,703
Isn't it just water?

1666
01:06:48,105 --> 01:06:51,307
- Does it taste like broth?
- A little bit.

1667
01:06:51,308 --> 01:06:52,309
It has a little bit of flavor.

1668
01:06:52,310 --> 01:06:54,777
I can feel a little bit of spice.
It must taste good then.

1669
01:06:55,278 --> 01:06:58,113
Dip the cooked ingredients in this sauce.

1670
01:07:00,884 --> 01:07:02,618
Thank you.

1671
01:07:02,619 --> 01:07:05,454
I think this is the hotpot sauce.

1672
01:07:05,455 --> 01:07:07,356
- The dipping sauce.
- Yes.

1673
01:07:07,357 --> 01:07:08,624
Chili sauce.

1674
01:07:08,625 --> 01:07:10,192
This is so interesting.

1675
01:07:10,193 --> 01:07:12,761
It really is a combination of barbecue...

1676
01:07:12,762 --> 01:07:14,530
- and hotpot.
- Interesting.

1677
01:07:14,664 --> 01:07:16,031
- Let's grill the meat.
- Shall we?

1678
01:07:16,366 --> 01:07:18,334
Let me try it first.

1679
01:07:18,668 --> 01:07:21,637
(Sizzle)

1680
01:07:22,005 --> 01:07:23,006
(A familiar sound of home, far from home.)

1681
01:07:23,007 --> 01:07:25,007
- That looks so yummy.
- So yummy.

1682
01:07:25,642 --> 01:07:28,277
I think it cooks fast...

1683
01:07:28,712 --> 01:07:30,146
because it's sliced pretty thin.

1684
01:07:31,448 --> 01:07:33,682
It smells exactly like Korean barbecue.

1685
01:07:33,850 --> 01:07:34,750
I can smell pork belly.

1686
01:07:34,884 --> 01:07:36,084
It's like shaved pork belly.

1687
01:07:36,687 --> 01:07:39,588
Somewhere between regular
and shaved pork belly.

1688
01:07:39,589 --> 01:07:40,489
- Right?
- Right.

1689
01:07:41,624 --> 01:07:42,891
Hotpot...

1690
01:07:43,193 --> 01:07:45,027
and grilled pork all at once.

1691
01:07:45,528 --> 01:07:46,361
It looks so good.

1692
01:07:46,362 --> 01:07:48,063
The pork grease
naturally falls into the broth.

1693
01:07:48,064 --> 01:07:50,999
Yeah. I bet it tastes nice and light.

1694
01:07:52,135 --> 01:07:53,435
Wow, it looks amazing.

1695
01:07:54,904 --> 01:07:56,972
Shall we try this?

1696
01:07:56,973 --> 01:07:58,740
We got exactly four pieces cooked.

1697
01:07:58,741 --> 01:07:59,774
Alright!

1698
01:08:01,044 --> 01:08:02,845
Do we need to dip it in sauce, or not?

1699
01:08:03,380 --> 01:08:04,513
- Is it good?
- It's so good.

1700
01:08:05,348 --> 01:08:06,381
- Dip it in sauce?
- Yeah.

1701
01:08:06,950 --> 01:08:09,818
They put a lot of pepper on it.

1702
01:08:09,819 --> 01:08:11,320
Yes. It's perfectly seasoned.

1703
01:08:12,822 --> 01:08:13,989
I can eat these like a vacuum.

1704
01:08:13,990 --> 01:08:15,457
(Sian also takes a big bite.)

1705
01:08:18,128 --> 01:08:20,029
Seriously, it's so good.

1706
01:08:20,030 --> 01:08:20,930
Really?

1707
01:08:22,031 --> 01:08:24,633
(It's sweet yet light,
with an extra savory kick...)

1708
01:08:25,435 --> 01:08:26,501
(if you dip it in a chili sauce!)

1709
01:08:26,502 --> 01:08:28,370
- It's so good.
- Right?

1710
01:08:28,938 --> 01:08:31,172
This is some really good meat.

1711
01:08:31,674 --> 01:08:33,208
I think it's pork belly.

1712
01:08:33,209 --> 01:08:34,609
This is pretty good meat.

1713
01:08:34,610 --> 01:08:35,844
It's so thin.

1714
01:08:36,746 --> 01:08:39,815
And it's not too thin.

1715
01:08:39,816 --> 01:08:41,950
- So it's got a nice bite to it.
- Totally. It's so chewy.

1716
01:08:41,951 --> 01:08:44,252
- It's nice and chewy.
- It cooks fast too.

1717
01:08:44,253 --> 01:08:45,286
(The texture is tender and chewy.)

1718
01:08:45,287 --> 01:08:46,588
It's perfect.

1719
01:08:48,825 --> 01:08:51,827
Eating outside like this...

1720
01:08:51,828 --> 01:08:53,896
kinda feels like camping.

1721
01:08:53,897 --> 01:08:55,731
It's not that hot today.

1722
01:08:55,932 --> 01:08:57,466
It's not hot. The weather's perfect.

1723
01:08:57,467 --> 01:08:59,968
People eat pork belly outdoors
like this a lot these days.

1724
01:09:00,236 --> 01:09:02,604
- That's right.
- Outdoors pork belly.

1725
01:09:02,605 --> 01:09:04,172
We have our butterfly friends,

1726
01:09:04,673 --> 01:09:06,308
and our tinkerbell friends
enjoying with us.

1727
01:09:06,409 --> 01:09:08,343
There are so many tinkerbells.

1728
01:09:08,945 --> 01:09:09,811
Tinkerbell!

1729
01:09:10,280 --> 01:09:11,880
This is insanely good.

1730
01:09:11,881 --> 01:09:12,715
- For real.
- So good.

1731
01:09:13,150 --> 01:09:14,283
I'm definitely going to miss this.

1732
01:09:14,851 --> 01:09:15,717
Me too.

1733
01:09:16,119 --> 01:09:17,619
Who knew we'd be doing this in Thailand?

1734
01:09:17,620 --> 01:09:18,554
I know, right?

1735
01:09:18,755 --> 01:09:20,022
This is such a vibe.

1736
01:09:20,924 --> 01:09:23,492
We have our elephant wake-up call
tomorrow.

1737
01:09:23,493 --> 01:09:25,294
"Elephant wake-up call."

1738
01:09:25,295 --> 01:09:27,496
- Are they calling us?
- Elephant wake-up call!

1739
01:09:27,497 --> 01:09:29,098
Are they going to call us?

1740
01:09:29,099 --> 01:09:30,766
The elephant's coming at 8 a.m.

1741
01:09:31,768 --> 01:09:32,801
At 8 a.m.?

1742
01:09:32,802 --> 01:09:34,570
Will they knock on the door
with their trunks?

1743
01:09:34,804 --> 01:09:36,338
I have no idea how they do it.

1744
01:09:36,339 --> 01:09:37,572
I'm excited.

1745
01:09:37,807 --> 01:09:39,808
- Maybe they'll spray water on us.
- I can't wait to see.

1746
01:09:39,809 --> 01:09:41,643
- "Hey, wake up!"
- Breaking my eardrum.

1747
01:09:41,644 --> 01:09:43,211
If that happens, I'm done with elephants.

1748
01:09:43,313 --> 01:09:44,280
Instant goodbye.

1749
01:09:44,514 --> 01:09:46,882
But don't you wake up before that?

1750
01:09:47,050 --> 01:09:49,118
I wake up earlier than you think.

1751
01:09:49,119 --> 01:09:50,152
- You do.
- Yeah.

1752
01:09:50,153 --> 01:09:51,553
I'm a morning person.

1753
01:09:51,821 --> 01:09:53,388
- You really don't sleep that much.
- Right.

1754
01:09:53,389 --> 01:09:55,190
Because I want to wash my hair
in the morning.

1755
01:09:56,159 --> 01:09:57,660
But you washed it in the evening today.

1756
01:09:57,661 --> 01:09:58,927
So I'm not going to wash it tomorrow.

1757
01:09:59,162 --> 01:10:00,629
How about you sleep in a little tomorrow?

1758
01:10:00,630 --> 01:10:01,930
- Have a deep sleep tonight.
- Yes, I will.

1759
01:10:02,165 --> 01:10:04,066
I think waking up to an elephant
knocking on the door...

1760
01:10:04,067 --> 01:10:05,868
- would be a pretty good way to wake up.
- Totally.

1761
01:10:05,869 --> 01:10:06,702
Agreed.

1762
01:10:06,903 --> 01:10:08,171
It'd be so cool.

1763
01:10:08,172 --> 01:10:09,773
If I'm already awake,

1764
01:10:09,774 --> 01:10:11,540
- the elephant might be a little confused.
- Sure.

1765
01:10:11,541 --> 01:10:13,442
Yes. It might leave.

1766
01:10:13,443 --> 01:10:14,543
"Hmm? She's already up."

1767
01:10:14,878 --> 01:10:15,778
(Elephant leaves with a trunk twirl.)

1768
01:10:15,779 --> 01:10:16,645
- It'd be meaningless.
- Right?

1769
01:10:16,946 --> 01:10:18,513
(Goodbye, girls!)

1770
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:20,583
Don't set up your alarms.

1771
01:10:20,783 --> 01:10:23,184
- Let's not wake up until they arrive!
- Deal!

1772
01:10:23,185 --> 01:10:25,320
Even if you're awake, don't get up.

1773
01:10:25,321 --> 01:10:26,955
Go back to sleep.

1774
01:10:26,956 --> 01:10:28,590
- I don't want to disappoint the elephant.
- Me too.

1775
01:10:28,691 --> 01:10:29,758
It's the elephant's only job.

1776
01:10:29,759 --> 01:10:31,960
"I'm going to go surprise
those girls again!"

1777
01:10:31,961 --> 01:10:32,961
That's probably what it'll be thinking.

1778
01:10:33,162 --> 01:10:34,629
Alright. For the elephant.

1779
01:10:34,630 --> 01:10:35,396
- Okay.
- Okay.

1780
01:10:35,397 --> 01:10:36,965
Abra-ca-Empty!

1781
01:10:36,966 --> 01:10:38,133
(Full bellies,
and now the chatter begins.)

1782
01:10:38,134 --> 01:10:40,168
Abra-ca-Empty!

1783
01:10:40,903 --> 01:10:42,337
(Goofing around)

1784
01:10:42,338 --> 01:10:43,104
So cute!

1785
01:10:44,207 --> 01:10:46,208
This tastes like jelly, don't you think?

1786
01:10:46,209 --> 01:10:48,243
(A relaxing end to a lovely dinner.)

1787
01:10:53,917 --> 01:10:56,085
How much is it?

1788
01:10:56,086 --> 01:10:57,186
Why? What's wrong?

1789
01:10:57,621 --> 01:10:58,687
You skipped out on the bill.

1790
01:10:58,688 --> 01:10:59,587
What?

1791
01:11:00,256 --> 01:11:01,556
This is supposed to be my personal budget.

1792
01:11:01,557 --> 01:11:02,324
(Almost became a dine-and-dasher.)

1793
01:11:02,825 --> 01:11:04,659
They all left...

1794
01:11:04,660 --> 01:11:07,095
while I was in the restroom.
And apparently, no one paid.

1795
01:11:07,096 --> 01:11:08,563
So I had to pay with my own money.

1796
01:11:08,865 --> 01:11:10,065
How much is it again?

1797
01:11:10,300 --> 01:11:12,234
It's 1,119 baht.

1798
01:11:12,235 --> 01:11:13,068
Wait.

1799
01:11:13,369 --> 01:11:15,170
I only have a little over 2,000.

1800
01:11:16,105 --> 01:11:17,005
I guess I have enough.

1801
01:11:17,006 --> 01:11:18,073
(Luckily, she can pay.)

1802
01:11:18,408 --> 01:11:19,575
Hi.

1803
01:11:19,576 --> 01:11:22,177
(Off goes the oldest to settle the bill.)

1804
01:11:22,312 --> 01:11:24,146
It feels kinda weird
asking to pay me back.

1805
01:11:24,548 --> 01:11:25,314
(Hesitating)

1806
01:11:25,315 --> 01:11:26,248
Should I just treat them, or not?

1807
01:11:27,050 --> 01:11:29,051
I'll pay for now,
and if I'm feeling generous, it's on me.

1808
01:11:29,052 --> 01:11:30,486
I just might.

1809
01:11:30,487 --> 01:11:31,453
Okay.

1810
01:11:31,454 --> 01:11:32,388
(Pays 1,119 baht out of her own pocket.)

1811
01:11:32,389 --> 01:11:35,257
Is 1,119 baht around 50 dollars?

1812
01:11:35,692 --> 01:11:38,394
Thank you.

1813
01:11:39,762 --> 01:11:42,598
Dear sisters, you probably don't know
you skipped the bill.

1814
01:11:42,599 --> 01:11:44,766
Maybe you'll never find out.

1815
01:11:45,168 --> 01:11:46,035
It's my treat.

1816
01:11:46,469 --> 01:11:47,502
I'm broke now.

1817
01:11:48,104 --> 01:11:49,705
I can't buy clothes tomorrow.

1818
01:11:50,174 --> 01:11:53,175
I lent them my clothes,
and now I'm doing this too.

1819
01:11:54,077 --> 01:11:56,145
They'll know
when they watch the show, right?

1820
01:11:57,532 --> 01:11:58,481
Okay.

1821
01:11:59,739 --> 01:12:04,157
(What will happen tomorrow?)

1822
01:12:05,937 --> 01:12:08,797
(The morning of Day 5 with the elephants)

1823
01:12:09,158 --> 01:12:11,330
(They woke up, and there's
an elephant right in front of them.)

1824
01:12:11,777 --> 01:12:12,862
An elephant...

1825
01:12:12,963 --> 01:12:14,597
I'll give you some food.

1826
01:12:14,990 --> 01:12:18,943
- It's not really a morning wake-up call.
- It's more like a morning feeding.

1827
01:12:20,537 --> 01:12:23,723
(The third destination
of the trip is revealed.)

1828
01:12:23,870 --> 01:12:25,477
(A jungle village?)

1829
01:12:25,811 --> 01:12:27,917
Are we supposed to live like monkeys?

1830
01:12:28,144 --> 01:12:31,064
(The four are left in shock.)

1831
01:12:31,224 --> 01:12:33,331
(Suddenly, they have some free time?)

1832
01:12:33,504 --> 01:12:35,251
Then let's make today our glam day.

1833
01:12:35,431 --> 01:12:37,909
(They finally get a day
to dress up Won Ji.)

1834
01:12:37,995 --> 01:12:40,075
My style inspiration is Cardi B.

1835
01:12:40,229 --> 01:12:42,291
This is amazing.

1836
01:12:42,449 --> 01:12:46,049
(A traditional outfit
with the glamour turned all the way up)

1837
01:12:46,382 --> 01:12:48,033
(All kinds of sparkles
make their grand appearance)

1838
01:12:48,240 --> 01:12:51,960
(The peacock is already losing its mind.)

1839
01:12:52,253 --> 01:12:56,047
(Their true self finally comes out
on Day 5 of the trip.)

1840
01:12:56,313 --> 01:12:57,960
(Roar)

1841
01:12:58,133 --> 01:12:59,913
(And today's highlight)

1842
01:13:00,093 --> 01:13:02,053
(The long-awaited Won Ji makeover)

1843
01:13:02,247 --> 01:13:04,113
(The younger ones bring out
all their styling skills)

1844
01:13:04,347 --> 01:13:06,067
(The final boss has appeared.)

1845
01:13:06,449 --> 01:13:08,383
(The creator is satisfied.)

1846
01:13:08,384 --> 01:13:09,664
You've totally changed.

1847
01:13:10,107 --> 01:13:12,047
(Did she successfully
transform into a hot girl?)

1848
01:13:12,247 --> 01:13:17,440
(Enjoying every minute of glam day)

1849
01:13:17,660 --> 01:13:20,187
(But it's exhausting.)

1850
01:13:20,580 --> 01:13:22,728
(It's time to pack again.)

1851
01:13:22,999 --> 01:13:24,302
Let's each take out at least one thing.

1852
01:13:24,768 --> 01:13:26,035
All right. No matter what.

1853
01:13:26,042 --> 01:13:27,668
I'm taking this one out.

1854
01:13:27,815 --> 01:13:29,415
- Are you throwing away a life?
- Yes.

1855
01:13:29,642 --> 01:13:32,701
(The fierce packing battle begins,
with the next travel budget on the line.)

1856
01:13:33,108 --> 01:13:33,543
(Thud)

1857
01:13:33,960 --> 01:13:34,972
Hold on.

1858
01:13:34,973 --> 01:13:36,180
Take your hands off it.

1859
01:13:36,546 --> 01:13:37,380
(Nervous)

1860
01:13:37,680 --> 01:13:41,226
(Can they actually manage
to reduce their luggage?)

1861
01:13:42,405 --> 01:13:44,405
Dramaday.me
